WEBVTT

00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:29.150
Damage report!

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:30.662
Shields at 60 percent.

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:32.961
Our fuel line has ruptured.
Attempting to compensate.

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:38.003
Damn it! We're barely
maintaining impulse.

00:00:38.038 --> 00:00:39.471
I can't get any more out of it.

00:00:39.506 --> 00:00:40.905
Be creative.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:42.567
How am I supposed to be creative

00:00:42.609 --> 00:00:44.440
with a 39-year-old
rebuilt engine?

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:47.173
Maquis ship

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:49.977
this is Gul Evek
of the Cardassian Fourth Order.

00:00:50.016 --> 00:00:52.484
Cut your engines and prepare
to surrender or we will de...

00:00:56.423 --> 00:00:59.221
Initiating evasive pattern
omega. Mark.

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:03.954
Shields at 50 percent.

00:01:03.997 --> 00:01:05.089
I need more power

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:06.758
if we're going to make
it to the Badlands.

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:07.960
Take the weapons off-line.

00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:09.969
We'll transfer all power
to the engines.

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:11.095
Considering the circumstances,

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:13.105
I'd question that proposal
at this time.

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:14.128
What does it matter?!

00:01:14.174 --> 00:01:17.234
We're not making a dent
in their shields anyway.

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:19.336
You wanted creative.

00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:21.347
Tuvok, shut down
all the phaser banks.

00:01:21.381 --> 00:01:23.815
If you can give me another
30 seconds at full impulse,

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.613
I'll get us into the Badlands.

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:27.279
Phasers off-line.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:29.151
Throw the last photons at them

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:31.919
and then give me the power
from the torpedo systems.

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:34.518
Acknowledged.
Firing photons.

00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:42.999
Are you reading
any plasma storms ahead?

00:01:43.036 --> 00:01:46.301
One.
Coordinates 171 mark 43.

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:48.264
That's where I'm going.

00:01:48.308 --> 00:01:51.209
Plasma storm density
increasing by 14 percent.

00:01:51.244 --> 00:01:52.905
Twenty...

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:54.413
Twenty-five...

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:55.505
Hold on!

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:05.182
Cardassian ship
is not reducing power.

00:02:05.225 --> 00:02:06.192
They're following us in.

00:02:06.226 --> 00:02:08.694
Gul Evek must feel daring today.

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:16.264
They've taken a hit
on their port blade.

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:17.963
They're sending out
a distress signal

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:19.732
on all Cardassian frequencies.

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:20.739
Can you plot a course

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:22.297
through these plasma fields,
Mr. Tuvok?

00:02:22.342 --> 00:02:25.243
Storm's activity is typically
widespread in this vicinity.

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:27.371
I can plot a course,
but I'm afraid it will require

00:02:27.413 --> 00:02:28.437
an indirect route.

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:30.210
We can use the time
to make some repairs.

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:32.842
What was that?

00:02:32.886 --> 00:02:33.978
Curious.

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:37.420
We just passed through some kind
of coherent tetryon beam.

00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:38.355
Source?

00:02:38.391 --> 00:02:39.380
Unknown.

00:02:40.393 --> 00:02:41.417
Now there appears to be

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:42.951
a massive displacement wave
moving toward us.

00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:44.463
Another storm?

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:46.158
It's not a plasma phenomenon.

00:02:46.199 --> 00:02:47.291
At current speeds

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:49.597
it will intercept us
in less than 30 seconds.

00:02:49.636 --> 00:02:52.002
Anything left in those
impulse generators, B'Elanna?

00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:53.094
We'll find out.

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:55.335
Still exceeding our speed.

00:02:55.375 --> 00:02:57.002
Maximum power.

00:02:57.043 --> 00:02:58.738
Wave is continuing
to accelerate.

00:02:58.778 --> 00:03:01.212
It will intercept us
in eight seconds.

00:03:03.049 --> 00:03:04.175
Five.

00:05:17.715 --> 00:05:19.444
Tom Paris?

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:24.445
Kathryn Janeway.

00:05:24.489 --> 00:05:26.957
I served with your father
on the Al-Batani.

00:05:26.991 --> 00:05:30.449
I wonder if we could
go somewhere and talk?

00:05:30.495 --> 00:05:32.326
About what?

00:05:32.363 --> 00:05:34.854
About a job we'd like
you to do for us.

00:05:34.899 --> 00:05:37.367
I'm already doing a job...

00:05:37.401 --> 00:05:38.766
for the Federation.

00:05:38.803 --> 00:05:40.668
I've been told
the Rehab Commission

00:05:40.705 --> 00:05:42.570
is very pleased with your work.

00:05:42.607 --> 00:05:45.974
They've given me their approval
to discuss this matter with you.

00:05:46.043 --> 00:05:48.978
Well, then I guess I'm yours.

00:05:52.750 --> 00:05:54.479
Your father taught me
a great deal.

00:05:54.519 --> 00:05:57.647
I was his Science Officer
during the Arias Expedition.

00:05:57.688 --> 00:05:59.679
You must be good.

00:05:59.724 --> 00:06:02.625
My father only accepts
the best and the brightest.

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:05.561
I'm leaving on a mission
to find a Maquis ship

00:06:05.596 --> 00:06:08.429
that disappeared in
the Badlands a week ago.

00:06:08.466 --> 00:06:10.661
I wouldn't, if I were you.

00:06:10.701 --> 00:06:12.032
Really?

00:06:12.069 --> 00:06:14.629
I've never seen
a Federation starship

00:06:14.672 --> 00:06:16.697
that could maneuver
through the plasma storms.

00:06:16.741 --> 00:06:19.073
You've never seen Voyager.

00:06:20.077 --> 00:06:21.738
We'd like you to come along.

00:06:23.214 --> 00:06:27.014
You'd like me to lead you
to my former colleagues.

00:06:28.352 --> 00:06:29.944
I was only with the Maquis
a few weeks

00:06:30.054 --> 00:06:31.419
before I was captured, Captain.

00:06:31.455 --> 00:06:34.185
I don't know where most
of their hiding places are.

00:06:34.225 --> 00:06:37.217
You know the territory
better than anyone we've got.

00:06:37.261 --> 00:06:40.753
What's so important about
this particular Maquis ship?

00:06:40.798 --> 00:06:44.290
My Chief of Security
was on board... undercover.

00:06:44.335 --> 00:06:47.429
He was supposed to report in
twice during the last six days.

00:06:47.471 --> 00:06:48.904
He didn't.

00:06:48.940 --> 00:06:52.171
Maybe it's just your Chief
of Security who's disappeared.

00:06:52.209 --> 00:06:54.575
Maybe.

00:06:55.746 --> 00:06:57.111
That ship was under the command

00:06:57.148 --> 00:06:58.172
of another former

00:06:58.215 --> 00:06:59.705
Starfleet officer

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:01.115
named Chakotay.

00:07:02.153 --> 00:07:04.348
I understand you knew him.

00:07:04.388 --> 00:07:06.913
That's right.

00:07:06.958 --> 00:07:10.223
The two of you didn't get along
too well, I'm told.

00:07:10.261 --> 00:07:13.128
Chakotay will tell you
he left Starfleet on principle...

00:07:13.164 --> 00:07:16.793
to defend his home colony
from the Cardassians.

00:07:16.834 --> 00:07:19.098
I, on the other hand,
was forced to resign.

00:07:19.136 --> 00:07:21.297
He considered me a mercenary...

00:07:21.339 --> 00:07:24.172
willing to fight for anyone
who'd pay my bar bills.

00:07:24.208 --> 00:07:27.177
The trouble is he was right.

00:07:30.348 --> 00:07:32.316
I have no problem helping you

00:07:32.350 --> 00:07:35.513
track down my "friends"
in the Maquis, Captain.

00:07:35.553 --> 00:07:39.182
All I need to know from you
is what's in it for me?

00:07:39.223 --> 00:07:41.054
You help us find that ship

00:07:41.092 --> 00:07:44.186
we help you
at your next outmate review.

00:07:44.228 --> 00:07:46.162
Uh-huh.

00:07:46.197 --> 00:07:47.391
Officially, you'd be

00:07:47.431 --> 00:07:49.456
a Starfleet observer
during the mission.

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:51.127
Observer?!

00:07:52.603 --> 00:07:55.163
Oh, hell, I'm the best pilot
you could have.

00:07:55.206 --> 00:07:57.106
You'll be an observer.

00:07:57.141 --> 00:08:00.167
When it's over,
you're cut loose.

00:08:00.211 --> 00:08:02.736
Story of my life.

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:19.855
Stadi, you're changing
my mind about Betazoids.

00:08:19.897 --> 00:08:21.660
Good.

00:08:21.699 --> 00:08:23.667
Oh, that wasn't a compliment.

00:08:23.701 --> 00:08:29.037
Until today, I always considered
your people warm and sensual.

00:08:29.073 --> 00:08:31.940
I can be warm and sensual.

00:08:32.009 --> 00:08:33.306
Just not to me.

00:08:33.344 --> 00:08:36.370
Do you always fly at women
at warp speed, Mr. Paris?

00:08:36.414 --> 00:08:39.178
Only when they're
in visual range.

00:08:41.786 --> 00:08:43.879
That's our ship.

00:08:43.921 --> 00:08:45.513
That's Voyager.

00:08:45.556 --> 00:08:47.183
Intrepid-class...

00:08:47.224 --> 00:08:49.590
sustainable cruise
velocity of warp factor

00:08:49.627 --> 00:08:51.754
9.975.

00:08:51.796 --> 00:08:55.960
15 decks,
crew complement of 141.

00:08:56.000 --> 00:08:57.968
Bio-neural circuitry.

00:08:58.069 --> 00:08:59.627
Bio-neural?

00:08:59.670 --> 00:09:00.762
Some of the traditional

00:09:00.805 --> 00:09:03.365
circuitry has been
replaced by gel packs

00:09:03.407 --> 00:09:05.341
that contain bio-neural cells.

00:09:05.376 --> 00:09:07.640
They organize information
more efficiently...

00:09:07.678 --> 00:09:09.646
speed up response time.

00:09:32.036 --> 00:09:35.062
If I may say so,
it's been my special pleasure

00:09:35.106 --> 00:09:37.233
to see many new officers
like yourself

00:09:37.274 --> 00:09:39.037
come through these portals.

00:09:39.076 --> 00:09:42.204
Your parents must be
very proud, my boy.

00:09:42.246 --> 00:09:45.147
You know, on an occasion
like this...

00:09:45.182 --> 00:09:46.274
I'm really not interested.

00:09:46.317 --> 00:09:47.545
Interested?

00:09:47.585 --> 00:09:49.416
You were about to try
to sell me something, right?

00:09:49.453 --> 00:09:51.114
I was merely going to suggest

00:09:51.155 --> 00:09:53.316
that your parents
might appreciate a memento

00:09:53.357 --> 00:09:54.324
of your first mission.

00:09:54.358 --> 00:09:56.826
And you happen to have several
to choose from?

00:09:56.861 --> 00:09:59.625
I do carry a select line

00:09:59.663 --> 00:10:02.291
of unique artifacts
and gemstones

00:10:02.333 --> 00:10:04.062
indigenous to this region.

00:10:04.101 --> 00:10:08.197
Why, quite recently,
I acquired these Lobi crystals

00:10:08.239 --> 00:10:11.299
from a very strange creature
called a Morn.

00:10:11.342 --> 00:10:13.902
We were warned about the Ferengi
at the Academy.

00:10:14.912 --> 00:10:16.971
Warned about Ferengi, were you?

00:10:17.081 --> 00:10:18.446
That's right.

00:10:18.482 --> 00:10:21.974
Slurs about my people
at Starfleet Academy.

00:10:22.052 --> 00:10:22.984
What I meant was...

00:10:23.087 --> 00:10:26.750
Here I am, trying to be
a cordial host, knowing

00:10:26.791 --> 00:10:29.783
how much a young officer's
parents would appreciate

00:10:29.827 --> 00:10:32.955
a token of his love on the eve
of a dangerous mission

00:10:32.997 --> 00:10:35.124
and what do I get
for my trouble?

00:10:35.166 --> 00:10:37.327
Scurrilous insults.

00:10:37.368 --> 00:10:40.997
Well, somebody's
going to hear about this.

00:10:41.038 --> 00:10:43.336
What's your name, son?

00:10:43.374 --> 00:10:45.308
My... name?

00:10:45.342 --> 00:10:46.468
You have one, I presume?

00:10:46.510 --> 00:10:47.670
Kim, Harry Kim, but I...

00:10:47.711 --> 00:10:48.735
And who was it

00:10:48.779 --> 00:10:51.646
at the Academy who warned you
about Ferengi?

00:10:51.682 --> 00:10:53.411
You know, I think
a memento for my parents

00:10:53.450 --> 00:10:54.417
would be a great idea.

00:10:54.451 --> 00:10:55.918
Oh, no, no, no, no,
no, no, no, no!

00:10:55.953 --> 00:10:57.682
Really, one of these

00:10:57.721 --> 00:10:59.188
would make a great pendant
for my mother.

00:10:59.223 --> 00:11:00.485
Or cufflinks for your father.

00:11:00.524 --> 00:11:02.515
Cufflinks.
Great idea.

00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:04.391
They're not for sale.

00:11:04.428 --> 00:11:08.296
Now, inform
your commanding officer

00:11:08.332 --> 00:11:12.200
that the Federation Council
can expect an official query...

00:11:12.236 --> 00:11:13.863
How much for the entire tray?

00:11:16.040 --> 00:11:17.530
Cash or credit?

00:11:17.575 --> 00:11:19.440
Dazzling, aren't they?

00:11:19.476 --> 00:11:21.535
As bright as a Koladan diamond.

00:11:21.579 --> 00:11:22.876
Brighter.

00:11:22.913 --> 00:11:24.278
Hard to believe
you can find them

00:11:24.315 --> 00:11:25.577
on any planet in the system.

00:11:25.616 --> 00:11:26.674
That's an exaggeration.

00:11:26.717 --> 00:11:29.948
You know, there's a shop
at the Volnar Colony

00:11:29.987 --> 00:11:31.978
that sells
a dozen assorted shapes

00:11:32.022 --> 00:11:33.489
for one Cardassian lek.

00:11:33.524 --> 00:11:35.719
How much are you
selling these for?

00:11:35.759 --> 00:11:38.626
We were just about
to negotiate the price.

00:11:42.700 --> 00:11:43.758
Come on.

00:11:48.672 --> 00:11:50.139
Thanks.

00:11:50.174 --> 00:11:53.439
Didn't they warn you about
Ferengi at the Academy?

00:12:01.118 --> 00:12:03.746
Run a level-3 diagnostic
just to be sure.

00:12:05.890 --> 00:12:06.948
Can I help you?

00:12:07.057 --> 00:12:09.321
Tom Paris, reporting on board.

00:12:09.360 --> 00:12:10.759
Oh, yes.

00:12:10.794 --> 00:12:13.126
The observer.

00:12:13.163 --> 00:12:14.494
That's me.

00:12:16.734 --> 00:12:18.964
As a matter of fact,
I seem to be observing

00:12:19.003 --> 00:12:21.198
some kind of problem
right now...

00:12:21.238 --> 00:12:22.967
Doctor.

00:12:23.007 --> 00:12:26.909
I was a surgeon
at the hospital on Caldik Prime

00:12:26.944 --> 00:12:29.742
the same time you were
stationed there.

00:12:29.780 --> 00:12:31.304
We never actually met.

00:12:33.517 --> 00:12:34.950
Your medical records
have arrived

00:12:34.985 --> 00:12:36.509
from your last posting,
Mr. Paris.

00:12:36.553 --> 00:12:38.987
Everything seems to be
in order.

00:12:39.056 --> 00:12:41.786
The Captain asked
if you were on board.

00:12:41.825 --> 00:12:42.917
You should check in with her.

00:12:42.960 --> 00:12:44.359
Uh...

00:12:44.395 --> 00:12:46.420
I haven't paid my respects
to the Captain yet either.

00:12:46.463 --> 00:12:49.660
Well, Mr. Kim,
that would be a good thing

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:51.691
for a new
Operations Officer to do.

00:12:56.774 --> 00:12:57.934
What was that all about?

00:12:57.975 --> 00:12:59.101
It's a long story, Harry

00:12:59.143 --> 00:13:00.440
and I'm tired of telling it.

00:13:00.477 --> 00:13:02.707
I'm sure someone around here
will tell you before long.

00:13:03.747 --> 00:13:04.736
The doctor called.

00:13:04.782 --> 00:13:05.749
And?

00:13:05.783 --> 00:13:06.841
And I was right.

00:13:06.884 --> 00:13:08.044
She's pregnant?

00:13:08.085 --> 00:13:09.643
Puppies are due in seven weeks.

00:13:09.687 --> 00:13:11.120
Oh, Mark, you've got
to take her home with you.

00:13:11.155 --> 00:13:13.055
With me?

00:13:13.090 --> 00:13:14.455
I just got the rugs cleaned.

00:13:14.491 --> 00:13:15.480
She's with child.

00:13:15.526 --> 00:13:17.118
I can't leave her
in a kennel while I...

00:13:17.161 --> 00:13:19.789
Is this another "love me,
love my dog" demand?

00:13:19.830 --> 00:13:21.127
Yes.

00:13:21.165 --> 00:13:22.496
How could I ever refuse you?

00:13:22.533 --> 00:13:23.727
Thanks, honey.

00:13:23.767 --> 00:13:25.132
So when are you leaving?

00:13:25.169 --> 00:13:27.637
As soon as I approve
these system status reports.

00:13:27.671 --> 00:13:30.663
All right, then I won't
bother you anymore.

00:13:30.708 --> 00:13:32.141
Hey...

00:13:34.979 --> 00:13:36.879
you never bother me.

00:13:36.914 --> 00:13:39.815
Except the way I love
to be bothered.

00:13:39.850 --> 00:13:40.817
Understand?

00:13:40.851 --> 00:13:42.648
I'll remember that.

00:13:42.686 --> 00:13:44.415
See you in a few weeks.

00:13:44.455 --> 00:13:46.286
Oh, Mark, go by my house
and pick up the doggy bed.

00:13:46.323 --> 00:13:47.654
She'll be more comfortable.

00:13:47.691 --> 00:13:49.420
I already did.

00:13:49.460 --> 00:13:51.621
An hour ago.

00:14:01.605 --> 00:14:02.731
Come in.

00:14:06.076 --> 00:14:08.874
Gentlemen,
welcome aboard Voyager.

00:14:08.912 --> 00:14:09.901
Thank you, sir.

00:14:11.548 --> 00:14:13.277
Mr. Kim...

00:14:13.317 --> 00:14:15.979
at ease
before you sprain something.

00:14:17.254 --> 00:14:19.518
Ensign, despite
Starfleet protocol

00:14:19.556 --> 00:14:21.649
I don't like being
addressed as "sir."

00:14:21.692 --> 00:14:23.922
I'm sorry... ma'am.

00:14:23.961 --> 00:14:25.895
"Ma'am" is acceptable
in a crunch,

00:14:25.929 --> 00:14:27.521
but I prefer "Captain."

00:14:27.564 --> 00:14:29.930
We're getting ready to leave.

00:14:29.967 --> 00:14:31.457
Let me show you to the Bridge.

00:14:31.502 --> 00:14:34.164
Did you have any problems
getting here, Mr. Paris?

00:14:34.204 --> 00:14:36.297
None at all, Captain.

00:14:37.975 --> 00:14:40.967
My First Officer,
Lieutenant Commander Cavit.

00:14:41.078 --> 00:14:43.376
Ensign Kim, Mr. Paris.

00:14:43.414 --> 00:14:44.574
Welcome aboard.

00:14:51.722 --> 00:14:54.748
Ensign Kim,
this is your station.

00:14:56.193 --> 00:14:57.922
Would you like to take over?

00:14:57.961 --> 00:14:59.826
Yes, ma'am.

00:14:59.863 --> 00:15:02.195
It's not crunch time yet,
Mr. Kim.

00:15:02.232 --> 00:15:03.631
I'll let you know when.

00:15:08.404 --> 00:15:09.928
Lieutenant Stadi,
lay in the course

00:15:10.006 --> 00:15:12.031
and clear our departure
with Operations.

00:15:12.075 --> 00:15:14.475
Course entered,
Ops has cleared us.

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:16.273
Ready thrusters.

00:15:16.312 --> 00:15:17.472
Thrusters ready.

00:15:17.513 --> 00:15:19.572
Initiate launching sequence.

00:15:19.615 --> 00:15:21.947
Sequence underway.

00:15:21.984 --> 00:15:23.042
Engage.

00:16:03.993 --> 00:16:05.426
Tomato soup.

00:16:05.461 --> 00:16:08.760
There are 14 varieties
of tomato soup available

00:16:08.798 --> 00:16:12.256
from this replicator...
with rice, with vegetables,

00:16:12.301 --> 00:16:14.428
Bolian-style,
with pasta, with...

00:16:14.470 --> 00:16:15.437
Plain.

00:16:15.471 --> 00:16:17.701
Specify hot or chilled.

00:16:17.740 --> 00:16:19.037
Hot!

00:16:19.075 --> 00:16:21.543
Hot, plain tomato soup.

00:16:35.158 --> 00:16:36.147
There, you see?

00:16:36.192 --> 00:16:38.092
I told you
it wouldn't take long.

00:16:40.062 --> 00:16:41.393
Is it true?

00:16:41.430 --> 00:16:43.159
Was the accident my fault?

00:16:43.199 --> 00:16:44.860
Yes... pilot error...

00:16:44.901 --> 00:16:47.961
but it took me
a while to admit it.

00:16:50.173 --> 00:16:51.140
Ugh! 14 varieties

00:16:51.174 --> 00:16:53.904
and they can't even get
plain tomato soup right.

00:16:53.943 --> 00:16:56.070
They said you falsified reports.

00:16:56.112 --> 00:16:57.170
That's right.

00:16:57.213 --> 00:16:58.202
Why?

00:16:58.247 --> 00:17:00.147
What's the difference?
I lied.

00:17:00.183 --> 00:17:01.480
But then you came forward

00:17:01.517 --> 00:17:03.576
and you admitted
that it was your fault?

00:17:05.188 --> 00:17:08.021
I'll tell you the truth, Harry.

00:17:08.057 --> 00:17:11.220
All I had to do
was keep my mouth shut

00:17:11.260 --> 00:17:13.160
and I was home free...

00:17:13.196 --> 00:17:14.254
but I couldn't.

00:17:14.297 --> 00:17:17.494
The ghosts of those
three dead officers

00:17:17.533 --> 00:17:19.125
came to me
in the middle of the night

00:17:19.168 --> 00:17:21.102
and taught me
the true meaning of Christmas.

00:17:21.137 --> 00:17:23.537
So I confessed...

00:17:23.573 --> 00:17:27.703
worst mistake I ever made
but not my last.

00:17:27.743 --> 00:17:30.803
After they cashiered me
out of Starfleet,

00:17:30.847 --> 00:17:33.714
I went out looking for a fight
and found the Maquis,

00:17:33.749 --> 00:17:38.550
and on my first assignment,
I was caught.

00:17:38.588 --> 00:17:41.751
That must have been
especially tough for you,

00:17:41.791 --> 00:17:43.691
being the son of an admiral.

00:17:43.726 --> 00:17:48.163
Frankly, I think it was tougher
on my father than it was on me.

00:17:52.034 --> 00:17:53.296
Look.

00:17:53.336 --> 00:17:55.327
I know those guys told you
to stay away from me,

00:17:55.371 --> 00:17:56.963
and you know what?

00:17:57.073 --> 00:17:58.904
You ought to listen to them.

00:17:58.941 --> 00:18:02.399
I'm not exactly
a good-luck charm.

00:18:03.679 --> 00:18:05.977
I don't need anyone
to choose my friends for me.

00:18:07.650 --> 00:18:09.083
Janeway to Paris.

00:18:09.118 --> 00:18:10.483
Go ahead.

00:18:10.519 --> 00:18:11.645
Report to the Bridge.

00:18:11.687 --> 00:18:13.052
We're approaching the Badlands.

00:18:21.964 --> 00:18:25.161
The plasma storms were measured
at levels three and four.

00:18:25.201 --> 00:18:27.396
The Cardassians gave us
the last known heading

00:18:27.436 --> 00:18:30.098
of the Maquis ship,
and we have charts

00:18:30.139 --> 00:18:32.699
of the plasma storm activity
the day it disappeared.

00:18:32.742 --> 00:18:33.936
With a little help,

00:18:33.976 --> 00:18:35.807
we might be able to
approximate its course.

00:18:35.845 --> 00:18:36.812
I'd guess

00:18:36.846 --> 00:18:38.677
they were trying to get
to one of the M-Class

00:18:38.714 --> 00:18:40.773
planetoids in the Terikof Belt.

00:18:40.816 --> 00:18:42.374
That's beyond the Moriya system

00:18:42.418 --> 00:18:45.581
The plasma storms would have
forced them in this direction.

00:18:45.621 --> 00:18:47.816
Adjust our course to match.

00:18:47.857 --> 00:18:48.824
Aye, Captain.

00:18:48.858 --> 00:18:50.257
The Cardassians claim
they forced

00:18:50.293 --> 00:18:52.193
the Maquis ship
into a plasma storm

00:18:52.228 --> 00:18:53.661
where it was destroyed,

00:18:53.696 --> 00:18:55.561
but our probes haven't
picked up any debris.

00:18:55.598 --> 00:18:58.396
A plasma storm might not leave
any debris.

00:18:58.434 --> 00:18:59.833
We'd still be able to pick up

00:18:59.869 --> 00:19:01.632
a resonance trace
from the warp core.

00:19:01.671 --> 00:19:02.899
Captain.

00:19:03.005 --> 00:19:05.064
I'm reading a coherent
tetryon beam scanning us.

00:19:05.107 --> 00:19:06.802
Origin, Mr. Kim?

00:19:06.842 --> 00:19:07.866
I'm not sure.

00:19:07.910 --> 00:19:09.537
There's also a displacement wave
moving toward us.

00:19:09.578 --> 00:19:11.205
On screen.

00:19:13.416 --> 00:19:15.247
Analysis.

00:19:15.284 --> 00:19:18.151
Some kind of polarized
magnetic variation.

00:19:18.187 --> 00:19:20.917
We might be able to disperse it
with a graviton particle field.

00:19:20.990 --> 00:19:22.116
Do it.

00:19:22.158 --> 00:19:23.284
Red Alert.

00:19:23.326 --> 00:19:24.759
Move us away from it,
Lieutenant.

00:19:24.794 --> 00:19:27.820
New heading 41 mark 180.

00:19:32.368 --> 00:19:34.563
Initiating graviton field.

00:19:37.306 --> 00:19:38.864
The graviton field
had no effect.

00:19:38.908 --> 00:19:41.001
Full impulse.

00:19:45.047 --> 00:19:46.708
The wave will intercept us
in 12 seconds.

00:19:46.749 --> 00:19:48.273
Can we go to warp?

00:19:48.317 --> 00:19:50.615
Not until we clear
the plasma field, Captain.

00:19:50.653 --> 00:19:52.621
Five seconds.

00:19:52.655 --> 00:19:54.179
Brace for impact.

00:19:54.223 --> 00:19:55.053
Three...

00:20:31.193 --> 00:20:32.251
Report.

00:20:33.562 --> 00:20:34.927
Hull breach, deck 14.

00:20:34.964 --> 00:20:36.261
Com lines
to Engineering are down.

00:20:36.298 --> 00:20:37.595
Trying to reestablish.

00:20:39.902 --> 00:20:43.167
Repair crews, seal off
hull breach on deck 14.

00:20:43.205 --> 00:20:44.263
Aye, Captain.

00:20:44.306 --> 00:20:46.297
Casualty reports coming in.

00:20:46.342 --> 00:20:48.003
Sick Bay is not responding.

00:20:48.044 --> 00:20:49.136
Bridge to Sick Bay.

00:20:49.178 --> 00:20:50.702
Doctor, can you hear me?

00:20:51.814 --> 00:20:53.839
Paris, how's Stadi?

00:20:53.883 --> 00:20:55.851
She's dead.

00:20:55.885 --> 00:20:57.216
Captain, there's
something out there.

00:20:57.253 --> 00:20:59.949
I need a better description
than that, Mr. Kim.

00:20:59.989 --> 00:21:01.081
I don't know.

00:21:01.123 --> 00:21:02.454
I'm reading...

00:21:02.491 --> 00:21:03.822
I'm not sure what I'm reading.

00:21:03.859 --> 00:21:05.690
Can you get
the viewscreen operational?

00:21:05.728 --> 00:21:07.252
I'm trying.

00:21:20.943 --> 00:21:24.106
Captain,
if these sensors are working

00:21:24.146 --> 00:21:27.115
we're over 70,000 light-years
from where we were.

00:21:27.149 --> 00:21:30.016
We're on the other side
of the galaxy.

00:21:41.363 --> 00:21:43.831
I'm not reading any life signs
on the Maquis ship.

00:21:43.866 --> 00:21:46.528
What about on that...
that Array?

00:21:46.569 --> 00:21:48.469
Our sensors can't penetrate it.

00:21:48.504 --> 00:21:49.835
Any idea what those pulses are

00:21:49.872 --> 00:21:51.362
that are coming from it,
Mr. Kim?

00:21:51.407 --> 00:21:52.533
Massive bursts
of radiant energy.

00:21:52.575 --> 00:21:53.599
They seem to be directed

00:21:53.642 --> 00:21:55.132
toward a nearby
G-type star system.

00:21:55.177 --> 00:21:56.804
Try hailing the Array.

00:21:56.846 --> 00:21:58.336
Engineering to Bridge.

00:21:58.380 --> 00:22:00.473
We have severe damage.
The chief's dead.

00:22:00.516 --> 00:22:02.381
Possibility
of a warp core breach.

00:22:02.418 --> 00:22:05.046
Secure all engineering systems.
I'm on my way.

00:22:05.087 --> 00:22:06.179
No response from the Array.

00:22:06.222 --> 00:22:07.951
Ensign, get down to Sick Bay.
See what's going on.

00:22:07.990 --> 00:22:09.389
Mr. Rollins,
the Bridge is yours.

00:22:09.425 --> 00:22:10.949
Aye, Captain.

00:22:14.797 --> 00:22:16.128
Harry, wait for me.

00:22:33.349 --> 00:22:34.407
They must have been

00:22:34.450 --> 00:22:36.111
right next to the console
when it exploded.

00:22:48.531 --> 00:22:51.796
Warning.
Warp core micro-fracture.

00:22:51.834 --> 00:22:53.199
Breach imminent.

00:22:54.336 --> 00:22:56.270
What's the warp core pressure?

00:22:56.305 --> 00:22:57.829
2,100 kilopascals.

00:22:59.074 --> 00:23:01.634
Lock down
the magnetic constrictors.

00:23:01.677 --> 00:23:03.941
If we lock them down
at these pressure levels,

00:23:03.979 --> 00:23:05.446
we might not be able
to reinitialize

00:23:05.481 --> 00:23:06.448
the dilithium reaction.

00:23:06.482 --> 00:23:07.676
Warning.

00:23:07.716 --> 00:23:09.547
Warp core microfracture.
Breach imminent.

00:23:09.585 --> 00:23:10.552
We don't have a choice.

00:23:10.586 --> 00:23:11.780
We've got to get
the reaction rate

00:23:11.820 --> 00:23:13.845
down
before we try to seal it.

00:23:14.823 --> 00:23:15.790
Computer, initiate

00:23:15.824 --> 00:23:17.485
emergency medical
holographic program.

00:23:20.496 --> 00:23:23.090
Please state the nature
of the medical emergency.

00:23:23.132 --> 00:23:24.292
Multiple percussive injuries.

00:23:24.333 --> 00:23:25.391
Status of your doctor?

00:23:25.434 --> 00:23:26.401
He's dead.

00:23:26.435 --> 00:23:27.732
.4cc's of trianoline.

00:23:27.770 --> 00:23:29.237
Trianoline?

00:23:29.271 --> 00:23:31.000
We lost our nurse, too.

00:23:32.441 --> 00:23:34.705
How soon are replacement
medical personnel expected?

00:23:34.743 --> 00:23:36.267
That could be a problem.

00:23:36.312 --> 00:23:38.337
We're pretty far away
from replacements right now.

00:23:40.049 --> 00:23:41.311
Tricorder.

00:23:45.788 --> 00:23:47.312
Medical tricorder.

00:23:55.698 --> 00:23:58.223
A replacement must be requested
as soon as possible.

00:23:58.267 --> 00:23:59.894
I am programmed
only as a short-term

00:23:59.935 --> 00:24:01.869
emergency supplement
to the medical team.

00:24:01.904 --> 00:24:04.896
Well, we may be stuck
with you for a while, Doc.

00:24:04.940 --> 00:24:06.601
There's no need for concern.

00:24:06.642 --> 00:24:09.270
I am capable of treating
any injury or disease.

00:24:09.311 --> 00:24:10.471
No concussion.
You'll be fine.

00:24:10.512 --> 00:24:11.536
Clean him up.

00:24:21.924 --> 00:24:23.789
Unlock the magnetic
constrictors.

00:24:28.464 --> 00:24:29.624
Constrictors on line.

00:24:29.665 --> 00:24:30.962
Pressure?

00:24:31.066 --> 00:24:32.124
It's working.

00:24:32.167 --> 00:24:35.159
2,500 kilopascals and holding.

00:24:35.204 --> 00:24:36.171
Bridge to Janeway.

00:24:36.205 --> 00:24:38.332
We're being scanned
by the Array, Captain.

00:24:38.374 --> 00:24:40.274
It's penetrated our shields.

00:24:40.309 --> 00:24:41.298
What kind of scan?

00:24:42.344 --> 00:24:43.311
Bridge?

00:24:43.345 --> 00:24:44.573
Janeway to Bridge.
Respond.

00:24:47.116 --> 00:24:48.981
Initiate emergency lock off.

00:24:56.258 --> 00:24:59.159
You're not seriously hurt.
You can return to your station.

00:25:09.405 --> 00:25:11.930
This is the emergency
holographic doctor speaking.

00:25:11.974 --> 00:25:12.941
I gave no permission

00:25:12.975 --> 00:25:15.000
for anyone to be transported
out of Sick Bay.

00:25:17.246 --> 00:25:18.645
Hello.

00:25:18.681 --> 00:25:20.273
Sick Bay to Bridge.

00:25:22.751 --> 00:25:25.549
I believe someone has failed
to terminate my program.

00:25:25.587 --> 00:25:26.781
Please respond.

00:25:41.070 --> 00:25:42.901
Come up here.

00:25:42.938 --> 00:25:43.905
Come on now.

00:25:43.939 --> 00:25:45.838
I have a pitcher

00:25:45.971 --> 00:25:48.337
of lemonade
and some sugar cookies.

00:25:53.979 --> 00:25:54.968
Captain?

00:25:55.013 --> 00:25:56.810
Don't believe your eyes,
Mr. Paris.

00:25:56.849 --> 00:25:58.976
We've only transported
100 kilometers.

00:25:59.051 --> 00:26:01.417
We're inside the Array.

00:26:01.453 --> 00:26:03.921
There's no indication
of stable matter.

00:26:03.956 --> 00:26:06.789
All this must be some kind
of holographic projection.

00:26:06.825 --> 00:26:09.157
Oh, you poor things.
You must be tired out.

00:26:09.194 --> 00:26:11.492
But come on and sit down
and rest a while.

00:26:11.530 --> 00:26:12.758
Have a cold drink, hmm?

00:26:12.798 --> 00:26:14.322
No, thank you.

00:26:14.366 --> 00:26:16.596
My name is Kathryn Janeway,

00:26:16.635 --> 00:26:19.195
Captain of the Federation
Starship Voyager.

00:26:19.238 --> 00:26:21.934
Now just make yourselves
right at home.

00:26:22.040 --> 00:26:24.372
The neighbors should
be here any minute.

00:26:24.409 --> 00:26:25.899
Oh. Why, here they are.

00:26:27.212 --> 00:26:28.179
Howdy.

00:26:28.213 --> 00:26:29.840
Welcome, folks.

00:26:29.882 --> 00:26:31.315
Hey.

00:26:31.350 --> 00:26:34.342
Well, good to see you.
Welcome.

00:26:34.386 --> 00:26:36.149
We're real glad you dropped by.

00:26:36.188 --> 00:26:37.951
Now we can get started.

00:26:37.990 --> 00:26:42.154
You're all invited
to the welcoming bee!

00:26:42.194 --> 00:26:43.957
Let's have some music!

00:26:49.968 --> 00:26:51.595
Yoo-hoo!

00:27:15.761 --> 00:27:18.594
The crew's scattered
around this farm, Captain,

00:27:18.630 --> 00:27:20.689
but they're all accounted for.

00:27:20.732 --> 00:27:22.893
Move around.
Scan the area.

00:27:22.935 --> 00:27:24.232
See if you can find anything

00:27:24.269 --> 00:27:26.169
that might be
a holographic generator.

00:27:27.839 --> 00:27:30.239
Have some nice fresh
corn on the cob.

00:27:30.275 --> 00:27:33.802
Fresh corn on the cob.

00:27:33.845 --> 00:27:37.303
Corn on the cob?
Corn on the cob?

00:27:37.349 --> 00:27:39.112
Can you tell me why we're here?

00:27:39.151 --> 00:27:41.142
Oh, we don't mean you any harm.

00:27:41.186 --> 00:27:43.677
I'm sorry if we've put you out.

00:27:43.722 --> 00:27:45.314
Why don't you just
put your feet up

00:27:45.357 --> 00:27:46.949
and get comfortable
while you wait?

00:27:47.059 --> 00:27:48.617
Wait for what?

00:27:48.660 --> 00:27:51.288
Isn't anybody hungry?

00:27:51.330 --> 00:27:53.594
Come on, now.
Make yourselves at home.

00:27:53.632 --> 00:27:55.930
I'm sorry if we've put you out.

00:28:07.980 --> 00:28:10.471
Hey, let me show you around.

00:28:10.515 --> 00:28:11.948
The root cellar's
right over there.

00:28:12.951 --> 00:28:14.077
What's down there?

00:28:14.119 --> 00:28:15.677
Potatoes, onions.

00:28:15.721 --> 00:28:17.450
But it's real private.

00:28:17.489 --> 00:28:18.820
Hmm.

00:28:18.857 --> 00:28:21.189
Paris, she's only a hologram.

00:28:21.226 --> 00:28:22.818
No reason to be rude.

00:28:24.029 --> 00:28:25.018
Whoa.

00:28:25.063 --> 00:28:26.030
What?

00:28:26.064 --> 00:28:27.554
Sporocystian life signs.

00:28:33.872 --> 00:28:35.362
What's in the barn?

00:28:35.407 --> 00:28:37.534
Oh, nothing
but a big ol' pile of hay.

00:28:37.576 --> 00:28:39.373
Hey, come on! Let's
go see the duck pond.

00:28:39.411 --> 00:28:40.378
Nothing in there.

00:28:40.412 --> 00:28:42.778
It's just a dark, smelly barn.

00:28:42.814 --> 00:28:45.544
Hey, do y'all want
some deviled eggs?

00:28:45.584 --> 00:28:46.915
Huh?

00:28:52.190 --> 00:28:54.715
See? Nothing but hay.

00:28:54.760 --> 00:28:56.352
There's a life-form here.

00:28:56.395 --> 00:28:57.919
- Just one.
- Where?

00:28:57.963 --> 00:28:59.089
It's everywhere.

00:29:00.332 --> 00:29:03.597
I'm also reading some kind
of matrix processing device.

00:29:03.635 --> 00:29:05.102
It may be
the holographic generator.

00:29:07.105 --> 00:29:08.868
Paris.

00:29:08.907 --> 00:29:10.772
Humanoid life signs over here.

00:29:10.809 --> 00:29:14.870
I'm reading a Vulcan
and several humans.

00:29:14.913 --> 00:29:17.609
I'm not ready for you yet!

00:29:23.388 --> 00:29:24.514
Paris to Janeway.

00:29:26.124 --> 00:29:27.091
Janeway here.

00:29:27.125 --> 00:29:28.319
Paris?

00:29:29.861 --> 00:29:30.850
Come on.

00:29:50.982 --> 00:29:51.949
Very well.

00:29:51.983 --> 00:29:54.645
Since no one seems
to care for any corn,

00:29:54.686 --> 00:29:57.211
we'll have to proceed
ahead of schedule.

00:31:27.879 --> 00:31:30.404
Janeway to Bridge.
Anybody there?

00:31:30.448 --> 00:31:32.439
Yes, Captain, we're here.

00:31:32.484 --> 00:31:33.849
How long were we over there?

00:31:35.720 --> 00:31:37.085
Almost three days.

00:31:37.122 --> 00:31:38.384
Three days!

00:31:38.423 --> 00:31:42.291
Captain, the Maquis ship
is powering up its engines.

00:31:42.327 --> 00:31:43.988
Tractor them.
All senior officers report

00:31:44.095 --> 00:31:45.289
to the Bridge immediately.

00:31:45.330 --> 00:31:48.595
Excuse me, could you explain
what has transpired?

00:31:48.633 --> 00:31:50.123
Computer, locate Ensign Kim.

00:31:50.168 --> 00:31:52.261
Ensign Kim is not on board.

00:31:52.304 --> 00:31:54.135
Uh, Paris to Janeway.

00:31:54.172 --> 00:31:55.969
Go ahead.

00:31:56.007 --> 00:31:58.237
Kim didn't come back with us.
He must still be over there.

00:31:58.276 --> 00:31:59.300
Acknowledged.

00:31:59.344 --> 00:32:01.209
Computer, how many crewmen
are unaccounted for?

00:32:01.246 --> 00:32:03.146
One: Ensign Harry Kim.

00:32:03.181 --> 00:32:04.648
Hail the Maquis.

00:32:06.284 --> 00:32:07.774
Commander Chakotay,

00:32:07.819 --> 00:32:10.287
my name is
Captain Kathryn Janeway.

00:32:10.322 --> 00:32:11.755
How do you know my name?

00:32:11.790 --> 00:32:13.257
We were on a mission
to find you

00:32:13.291 --> 00:32:15.156
when we were brought here
by the Array.

00:32:15.193 --> 00:32:17.320
One of our crewmen is missing.

00:32:17.362 --> 00:32:20.160
Was he transported back
to your ship by accident?

00:32:20.198 --> 00:32:23.099
No. A member of our crew
is missing, too.

00:32:23.134 --> 00:32:25.796
B'Elanna Torres, my Engineer.

00:32:25.837 --> 00:32:28.601
Commander, you and I
have the same problem.

00:32:28.640 --> 00:32:29.698
I think it makes sense

00:32:29.741 --> 00:32:31.709
to try and solve it together,
don't you?

00:32:37.115 --> 00:32:39.675
Three of us will transport
to your ship.

00:32:40.619 --> 00:32:41.984
They're powering down
their engines

00:32:42.053 --> 00:32:43.042
dropping their shields.

00:32:48.793 --> 00:32:50.226
Watch out, Captain.
They're armed.

00:32:51.363 --> 00:32:53.297
Put down your weapons.

00:32:55.967 --> 00:32:57.958
You won't need those here.

00:32:59.404 --> 00:33:01.235
It's good to have you back,
Mr. Tuvok.

00:33:02.874 --> 00:33:05.104
I must inform you
that I was assigned

00:33:05.143 --> 00:33:06.906
to infiltrate your crew, sir.

00:33:06.945 --> 00:33:09.277
I am Captain Janeway's
Chief of Security.

00:33:11.349 --> 00:33:13.078
Were you going to deliver us

00:33:13.118 --> 00:33:15.109
into their waiting hands,
Vulcan?

00:33:15.153 --> 00:33:18.247
My mission was
to accumulate information

00:33:18.290 --> 00:33:19.951
on Maquis activities

00:33:20.058 --> 00:33:22.856
and then deliver you
into their "waiting hands."

00:33:22.894 --> 00:33:23.861
That is correct.

00:33:23.895 --> 00:33:25.658
I see you had help.

00:33:25.697 --> 00:33:29.599
It's good to see you, too,
Chakotay.

00:33:29.634 --> 00:33:32.262
At least the Vulcan was doing
his duty as a Starfleet officer,

00:33:32.304 --> 00:33:33.566
but you...

00:33:33.605 --> 00:33:35.334
you betrayed us for what?

00:33:35.373 --> 00:33:38.570
Freedom from prison?
Latinum?

00:33:38.610 --> 00:33:40.976
What was your price this time?!

00:33:41.046 --> 00:33:43.105
You are speaking
to a member of my crew.

00:33:43.148 --> 00:33:45.207
I expect you to treat him
with the same respect

00:33:45.250 --> 00:33:47.650
as you would have me
treat a member of yours.

00:33:52.657 --> 00:33:56.388
Now, we have a lot to accomplish
and I suggest we all concentrate

00:33:56.428 --> 00:33:59.727
on finding our people
and getting ourselves back home.

00:33:59.764 --> 00:34:00.890
Based on my initial

00:34:00.932 --> 00:34:03.799
reconnaissance, Captain
I am convinced we are dealing

00:34:03.835 --> 00:34:05.826
with a single entity
in the Array.

00:34:05.870 --> 00:34:08.168
I would suggest
he scanned our computers

00:34:08.206 --> 00:34:11.334
in order to select a comfortable
holographic environment.

00:34:11.376 --> 00:34:13.310
In effect, a waiting room

00:34:13.345 --> 00:34:16.803
to pacify us prior
to biometric assessment.

00:34:16.848 --> 00:34:18.440
An examination?

00:34:18.483 --> 00:34:20.951
It is the most
logical explanation.

00:34:21.052 --> 00:34:23.316
Why else would he have
released us unharmed?

00:34:23.355 --> 00:34:25.585
Not all of us were.

00:34:27.425 --> 00:34:29.859
Break out the compression
phaser rifles.

00:34:29.894 --> 00:34:31.589
Meet us in Transporter Room 2.

00:34:31.629 --> 00:34:33.654
We're going back.

00:34:33.698 --> 00:34:35.461
We'll divide into teams.

00:34:35.500 --> 00:34:37.968
Mr. Tuvok, while Chakotay
and I are looking for Torres

00:34:38.069 --> 00:34:39.798
and, Kim, your job
is to find out

00:34:39.838 --> 00:34:42.306
as much about this Array
as you can.

00:34:42.340 --> 00:34:43.329
It brought us here.

00:34:43.375 --> 00:34:45.172
We have to assume
it can send us home.

00:34:45.210 --> 00:34:48.202
Agreed?

00:34:51.816 --> 00:34:54.478
Mr. Rollins, maintain Red Alert.

00:34:54.519 --> 00:34:56.612
Keep us on constant
transporter locks.

00:34:56.654 --> 00:34:57.643
Captain.

00:35:01.192 --> 00:35:02.352
I'd like to go with you.

00:35:02.394 --> 00:35:04.089
If this has something
to do with what Chakotay...

00:35:04.129 --> 00:35:06.359
It doesn't.
I just...

00:35:07.699 --> 00:35:10.167
I'd hate to see
anything happen to Harry.

00:35:12.237 --> 00:35:13.329
Come on.

00:35:36.828 --> 00:35:39.262
There are no humanoid
life-forms indicated, Captain.

00:35:39.297 --> 00:35:41.663
Kim and Torres are not
within tricorder range.

00:35:41.699 --> 00:35:43.223
They may not be on the Array.

00:35:43.268 --> 00:35:44.895
He can tell us where they are.

00:35:44.936 --> 00:35:46.699
Maintain your com link.

00:35:46.738 --> 00:35:48.899
I don't want
to lose anyone else.

00:36:01.352 --> 00:36:03.286
Oh, why have you come back?

00:36:03.321 --> 00:36:05.322
You don't have what I need.

00:36:05.455 --> 00:36:07.923
I don't know what you need
and, frankly, I don't care.

00:36:07.957 --> 00:36:09.390
I just want our people back

00:36:09.426 --> 00:36:11.326
and I want us all
to be sent home.

00:36:11.361 --> 00:36:14.194
Oh, well, now,
aren't you contentious

00:36:14.230 --> 00:36:17.028
for a minor bipedal species.

00:36:18.234 --> 00:36:20.293
This minor bipedal species

00:36:20.337 --> 00:36:22.396
doesn't take kindly
to being abducted.

00:36:22.439 --> 00:36:24.168
Oh, it was necessary.

00:36:24.207 --> 00:36:25.606
Where are our people?

00:36:25.642 --> 00:36:26.700
They are no longer here.

00:36:26.743 --> 00:36:28.142
What have you done to them?

00:36:28.178 --> 00:36:30.772
You don't have what I need.

00:36:30.814 --> 00:36:32.213
They might.

00:36:32.248 --> 00:36:33.647
No. You'll have to leave them.

00:36:33.683 --> 00:36:34.741
We won't do that.

00:36:34.784 --> 00:36:36.752
We are their commanding
officers.

00:36:36.786 --> 00:36:38.413
We are entrusted
with their safety.

00:36:38.455 --> 00:36:40.480
They are our responsibility.

00:36:40.523 --> 00:36:42.957
That may be a concept
you don't understand.

00:36:42.992 --> 00:36:46.393
Oh, no, I do understand,

00:36:46.429 --> 00:36:49.125
but I have no choice.

00:36:49.165 --> 00:36:51.895
Oh...

00:36:51.935 --> 00:36:54.961
There just is
not enough time left.

00:36:55.071 --> 00:36:56.698
Left for what?

00:36:56.740 --> 00:37:00.073
I must honor a debt
that can never be repaid,

00:37:00.110 --> 00:37:03.568
but my search has
not been going well.

00:37:07.016 --> 00:37:09.450
Tell us what you're looking for.

00:37:09.486 --> 00:37:11.249
Maybe we can help you find it.

00:37:11.287 --> 00:37:12.754
You?

00:37:14.524 --> 00:37:15.786
I've searched the galaxy

00:37:15.825 --> 00:37:17.884
with methods
beyond your comprehension.

00:37:17.927 --> 00:37:20.088
No. There's nothing you can do.

00:37:20.130 --> 00:37:23.896
You've taken us 70,000
light-years from our home.

00:37:23.933 --> 00:37:25.924
We have no way back
unless you send us

00:37:26.002 --> 00:37:27.936
and we won't leave
without the others.

00:37:28.004 --> 00:37:32.464
But... sending you back
is terribly complicated.

00:37:32.509 --> 00:37:33.942
Don't you understand?

00:37:34.010 --> 00:37:36.308
I don't have time.

00:37:36.346 --> 00:37:38.940
Not enough time!

00:38:08.011 --> 00:38:10.479
He's regaining consciousness.

00:38:12.282 --> 00:38:13.874
How do you feel?

00:38:15.351 --> 00:38:16.909
What am I doing here?

00:38:17.020 --> 00:38:18.112
Where am I?

00:38:18.154 --> 00:38:20.349
Please don't try to move yet.

00:38:20.390 --> 00:38:21.652
You're very ill.

00:38:21.691 --> 00:38:22.817
Ill? No, no,
there's some mistake,

00:38:22.859 --> 00:38:23.951
I'm not...

00:38:34.370 --> 00:38:35.496
No!

00:39:21.217 --> 00:39:25.449
Captain's Log, Stardate 48315.6.

00:39:25.488 --> 00:39:27.922
We've traced the energy pulses
from the Array

00:39:27.991 --> 00:39:30.789
to the fifth planet
of the neighboring system

00:39:30.827 --> 00:39:32.761
and believe they may have
been used in some fashion

00:39:32.795 --> 00:39:36.424
to transport Kim and Torres
to the planet's surface.

00:39:41.337 --> 00:39:42.668
Come in.

00:39:44.807 --> 00:39:48.470
Captain, I've observed something
peculiar about the pulses.

00:39:48.511 --> 00:39:50.376
They're getting faster.

00:39:51.881 --> 00:39:53.348
Faster.

00:39:53.383 --> 00:39:55.112
The interval between each pulse

00:39:55.151 --> 00:39:57.813
has decreased by.47
seconds since we arrived.

00:39:57.854 --> 00:39:59.822
I can offer no explanation.

00:39:59.856 --> 00:40:02.723
That's only one of the mysteries
we're dealing with, Mr. Tuvok.

00:40:02.759 --> 00:40:04.488
Take a look at this.

00:40:08.131 --> 00:40:10.429
It's virtually a desert.

00:40:10.466 --> 00:40:11.592
Not one ocean.

00:40:11.634 --> 00:40:12.828
Not one river.

00:40:12.869 --> 00:40:14.734
It has all the basic
characteristics

00:40:14.771 --> 00:40:16.398
of an M-Class planet, except...

00:40:18.041 --> 00:40:19.906
there are no
nucleogenic particles

00:40:19.943 --> 00:40:20.967
in the atmosphere.

00:40:21.010 --> 00:40:22.773
That would mean
the planet is incapable

00:40:22.812 --> 00:40:23.779
of producing rain.

00:40:23.813 --> 00:40:25.474
I've studied thousands
of M-Class planets.

00:40:25.515 --> 00:40:27.983
I've never seen an atmosphere
without nucleogenics.

00:40:28.017 --> 00:40:29.075
There must have been

00:40:29.118 --> 00:40:32.349
some kind of extraordinary
environmental disaster.

00:40:39.762 --> 00:40:41.730
As soon as repairs
are complete...

00:40:45.134 --> 00:40:47.728
we'll set a course
for the fifth planet.

00:40:52.075 --> 00:40:53.440
Captain.

00:40:53.476 --> 00:40:55.808
You require sleep.

00:40:57.380 --> 00:41:00.110
Kim's mother called me
just after he left Earth.

00:41:00.149 --> 00:41:02.083
Delightful woman.

00:41:02.118 --> 00:41:04.109
He's her only son.

00:41:04.153 --> 00:41:07.179
He'd left his clarinet behind.

00:41:07.223 --> 00:41:10.954
She wanted to know if she
had time to send it.

00:41:12.795 --> 00:41:14.194
I had to tell her no.

00:41:16.299 --> 00:41:18.199
Do you know
he played the clarinet

00:41:18.234 --> 00:41:20.099
in the Juilliard Youth Symphony?

00:41:20.136 --> 00:41:23.264
I did not have the opportunity
to meet Mr. Kim.

00:41:23.306 --> 00:41:25.740
I barely knew him.

00:41:27.677 --> 00:41:30.703
I never seem to have the chance
to get to know any of them.

00:41:33.082 --> 00:41:35.243
I have to, um...

00:41:37.020 --> 00:41:39.648
I have to take more time
to do that.

00:41:41.758 --> 00:41:44.784
It's a fine crew
and I've got to get them home.

00:41:47.163 --> 00:41:48.858
The crew will not benefit

00:41:48.898 --> 00:41:51.196
from the leadership
of an exhausted Captain.

00:41:54.003 --> 00:41:56.301
You're right as usual.

00:41:58.241 --> 00:41:59.868
I've missed your counsel, Tuvok.

00:41:59.909 --> 00:42:02.844
I am gratified
that you came after me

00:42:02.879 --> 00:42:04.574
so I can offer it once again.

00:42:04.614 --> 00:42:07.344
I spoke to your family
before I left.

00:42:07.383 --> 00:42:09.715
Are they well?

00:42:09.752 --> 00:42:12.277
Well, but worried about you.

00:42:12.321 --> 00:42:15.916
That would not be
an accurate perception, Captain.

00:42:15.958 --> 00:42:18.426
Vulcans do not worry.

00:42:18.461 --> 00:42:22.329
They... miss you.

00:42:24.033 --> 00:42:26.160
As I do them.

00:42:32.408 --> 00:42:34.308
I'll get you back to them.

00:42:34.343 --> 00:42:36.004
That's a promise, Tuvok.

00:42:49.092 --> 00:42:51.617
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:42:51.661 --> 00:42:54.755
The Maquis ship and Voyager
have encountered a debris field

00:42:54.797 --> 00:42:56.958
where sensors have detected
a small vessel.

00:42:56.999 --> 00:42:59.559
One humanoid life-form
is on board.

00:42:59.602 --> 00:43:01.297
Hail them.

00:43:11.380 --> 00:43:15.612
Whoever you are, I found
this waste zone first.

00:43:15.651 --> 00:43:18.848
We're not interested
in this debris, Mister?

00:43:18.888 --> 00:43:21.356
Neelix.

00:43:21.390 --> 00:43:25.952
And since you're not interested
in my "debris"

00:43:26.028 --> 00:43:28.963
well, I'm delighted to know you.

00:43:28.998 --> 00:43:30.556
Captain Kathryn Janeway

00:43:30.600 --> 00:43:33.125
of the Federation
Starship Voyager.

00:43:33.169 --> 00:43:34.966
A very impressive title.

00:43:35.004 --> 00:43:37.097
I have no idea what it means,

00:43:37.140 --> 00:43:38.971
but it sounds very impressive.

00:43:39.075 --> 00:43:43.273
Do you know this area
of space well, Mr. Neelix?

00:43:43.312 --> 00:43:46.247
I am famous for knowing it well.

00:43:46.282 --> 00:43:48.216
How may I be of service?

00:43:48.251 --> 00:43:50.151
Do you know anything
about the Array

00:43:50.186 --> 00:43:52.746
that's sending energy pulses
to the fifth planet?

00:43:52.789 --> 00:43:56.748
I know enough to stay
as far away from it as possible.

00:43:56.793 --> 00:44:00.456
Wait, let me guess.

00:44:00.496 --> 00:44:05.433
You were whisked away from
somewhere else in the galaxy

00:44:05.468 --> 00:44:07.868
and brought here
against your will.

00:44:07.904 --> 00:44:11.271
Sounds as though you've heard
this story before.

00:44:11.307 --> 00:44:14.538
Sadly, yes, thousands of times.

00:44:14.577 --> 00:44:16.442
Well, hundreds of times.

00:44:16.479 --> 00:44:18.606
Maybe 50 times.

00:44:18.648 --> 00:44:19.910
But the Caretaker

00:44:19.949 --> 00:44:22.941
has been bringing ships here
for months now.

00:44:23.019 --> 00:44:24.452
The Caretaker?

00:44:24.487 --> 00:44:28.048
That's what the Ocampa call him.

00:44:28.090 --> 00:44:30.957
They live on the fifth planet.

00:44:31.027 --> 00:44:34.827
Did he... kidnap members
of your crew?

00:44:34.864 --> 00:44:37.264
As a matter of fact, he did.

00:44:37.300 --> 00:44:39.666
It's not the first time.

00:44:39.702 --> 00:44:41.727
Do you know where
he might have taken them?

00:44:41.771 --> 00:44:44.797
Just that they're brought
to the Ocampa.

00:44:44.841 --> 00:44:46.741
Nothing more.

00:44:46.776 --> 00:44:48.607
We'd appreciate any help
you could give us

00:44:48.644 --> 00:44:50.908
in finding these... Ocampa.

00:44:50.947 --> 00:44:54.974
I-I-I really wish
that I could help you, I do.

00:44:55.017 --> 00:44:56.245
But as you can see,

00:44:56.285 --> 00:44:58.947
there's just so much debris
for me to investigate today.

00:44:58.988 --> 00:45:04.119
You'd be surprised the things
of value some people abandon.

00:45:04.160 --> 00:45:06.890
Of course, we'd want to
compensate you for your trouble.

00:45:06.929 --> 00:45:11.229
Well, there's really very little
that you could offer me.

00:45:11.267 --> 00:45:14.259
Unless...

00:45:14.303 --> 00:45:15.770
Yes?

00:45:15.805 --> 00:45:18.171
Unless, of course,

00:45:18.207 --> 00:45:20.266
you had...

00:45:20.309 --> 00:45:22.539
...water?

00:45:25.481 --> 00:45:28.245
If you help us find
our missing crew members,

00:45:28.284 --> 00:45:30.912
you can have
all the water you want.

00:45:32.855 --> 00:45:36.689
Well, tha-that sounds like
a very reasonable arrangement.

00:45:36.726 --> 00:45:38.091
Good. We'll beam you over

00:45:38.127 --> 00:45:39.856
and tow your ship
into our shuttlebay.

00:45:39.896 --> 00:45:43.423
Mr. Tuvok, go to Transporter
Room 2 and meet our guest.

00:45:43.466 --> 00:45:46.060
Beam?

00:45:46.102 --> 00:45:47.433
We have a technology

00:45:47.470 --> 00:45:50.371
which can take you instantly
from your ship to ours.

00:45:50.406 --> 00:45:52.169
It's quite harmless.

00:45:52.208 --> 00:45:53.505
May we?

00:45:59.916 --> 00:46:01.110
Energize.

00:46:11.826 --> 00:46:14.624
Astonishing!

00:46:14.662 --> 00:46:15.629
You Federations

00:46:15.663 --> 00:46:18.325
are obviously
an advanced culture.

00:46:18.366 --> 00:46:21.096
The Federation is made up
of many cultures.

00:46:21.135 --> 00:46:23.103
I am Vulcan.

00:46:23.137 --> 00:46:24.798
Neelix.

00:46:26.774 --> 00:46:28.639
Good to meet you.

00:46:28.676 --> 00:46:31.474
Interesting.

00:46:31.512 --> 00:46:35.380
What... what exactly...

00:46:37.485 --> 00:46:40.181
What exactly does all this...

00:46:40.221 --> 00:46:41.711
all this do?

00:46:41.756 --> 00:46:43.621
I assure you
that everything in this room

00:46:43.658 --> 00:46:45.888
has a specific function.

00:46:45.927 --> 00:46:49.488
However, it would take
several hours to explain it all.

00:46:49.530 --> 00:46:52.226
I suggest we proceed
to your quarters.

00:46:52.266 --> 00:46:53.995
Oh.

00:46:55.069 --> 00:46:57.162
Perhaps you would care
for a bath.

00:46:57.204 --> 00:46:58.933
A what?

00:46:58.973 --> 00:47:00.964
Hmm...

00:47:17.158 --> 00:47:19.592
It's okay.
It's okay.

00:47:19.627 --> 00:47:20.685
Who are you?

00:47:20.728 --> 00:47:23.595
My name is Kim... Harry Kim.

00:47:23.631 --> 00:47:25.189
I'm an Ensign
on the Starship Voyager.

00:47:25.232 --> 00:47:27.928
I was kidnapped from the Array
just like you were.

00:47:28.035 --> 00:47:29.161
I don't know where we are.

00:47:29.203 --> 00:47:31.034
What was Starfleet doing
at that Array?

00:47:31.072 --> 00:47:33.336
We were looking for you,
actually.

00:47:33.374 --> 00:47:35.399
One minute, we're, we're
in the Badlands, the next...

00:47:35.443 --> 00:47:37.570
You mean, you were
trying to capture us.

00:47:37.611 --> 00:47:40.079
Yeah... consider
yourself captured.

00:47:40.114 --> 00:47:41.809
Oh, I know I have
a phaser here somewhere.

00:47:41.849 --> 00:47:44.841
I don't find this
at all amusing, Starfleet.

00:47:47.755 --> 00:47:49.313
There's no point.

00:47:49.357 --> 00:47:51.416
It's locked.

00:47:52.927 --> 00:47:53.951
Hey!

00:47:53.995 --> 00:47:55.758
Hey, hey, hey what's that
going to accomplish?

00:47:55.796 --> 00:47:57.058
What are they doing to us?!

00:47:57.098 --> 00:47:58.565
What are these things
growing on us?!

00:47:58.599 --> 00:48:00.624
Look, do you want them
to sedate you again?

00:48:04.138 --> 00:48:06.538
You're right, Starfleet.

00:48:12.480 --> 00:48:14.573
It's the Klingon half of me.

00:48:14.615 --> 00:48:17.778
It's just, it's hard
to control it sometimes.

00:48:24.892 --> 00:48:26.450
What's your name, Maquis?

00:48:32.867 --> 00:48:34.630
B'Elanna.

00:48:34.668 --> 00:48:36.932
B'Elanna Torres.

00:48:38.973 --> 00:48:41.498
I hope you're feeling better.

00:48:41.542 --> 00:48:44.705
I know how frightening all this
must be for both of you.

00:48:44.745 --> 00:48:48.374
I've brought some clothes
if you care to change.

00:48:48.416 --> 00:48:50.441
Why are you holding us here?

00:48:50.484 --> 00:48:52.076
You are not prisoners.

00:48:52.119 --> 00:48:55.088
In fact,
we consider you honored guests.

00:48:56.657 --> 00:48:59.387
The Caretaker
has sent you to us.

00:48:59.427 --> 00:49:00.553
As long as you are not violent

00:49:00.594 --> 00:49:01.891
you are free
to leave your quarters.

00:49:01.996 --> 00:49:04.157
What's wrong with us?

00:49:04.198 --> 00:49:06.359
What are these things?

00:49:06.400 --> 00:49:08.891
We really don't know.

00:49:11.072 --> 00:49:12.664
You must be hungry.

00:49:12.706 --> 00:49:15.607
Would you care to join me
on the courtyard for a meal?

00:49:19.313 --> 00:49:21.679
Our food dispensers
are right this way.

00:49:25.553 --> 00:49:27.453
We're underground.

00:49:27.488 --> 00:49:30.218
Our society is subterranean.

00:49:30.257 --> 00:49:34.216
We've lived here
for over 500 generations.

00:49:34.261 --> 00:49:36.422
But before that,
you lived on the surface?

00:49:36.464 --> 00:49:38.261
Until the warming began.

00:49:38.299 --> 00:49:39.288
The warming?

00:49:39.333 --> 00:49:41.460
When our surface
turned into a desert

00:49:41.502 --> 00:49:44.062
and the Caretaker
came to protect us.

00:49:44.105 --> 00:49:47.097
Our ancient journals
tell us he opened

00:49:47.141 --> 00:49:48.768
a deep chasm in the ground

00:49:48.809 --> 00:49:51.243
and led our ancestors
to this place.

00:49:51.278 --> 00:49:54.839
Since then, he has provided
for all our needs.

00:49:59.653 --> 00:50:01.883
Oh, please forgive them.

00:50:01.922 --> 00:50:03.856
They know you've come
from the Caretaker.

00:50:03.891 --> 00:50:06.587
None of us has ever seen him.

00:50:06.627 --> 00:50:08.686
This way, please.

00:50:21.909 --> 00:50:24.343
Does the Caretaker
provide your meals, too?

00:50:24.378 --> 00:50:25.436
In fact, he does.

00:50:25.479 --> 00:50:26.776
He designed

00:50:26.814 --> 00:50:29.647
and built this entire city
for us after the warming.

00:50:29.683 --> 00:50:32.516
The food processors dispense
nutritional supplements

00:50:32.553 --> 00:50:34.544
every 4.1 intervals.

00:50:36.590 --> 00:50:38.990
It may not offer
the exotic tastes

00:50:39.026 --> 00:50:41.187
some of our younger people
crave these days,

00:50:41.228 --> 00:50:42.786
but it meets our needs.

00:50:46.901 --> 00:50:49.426
Is this how the Caretaker
communicates with you?

00:50:49.470 --> 00:50:51.700
He never communicates directly.

00:50:51.739 --> 00:50:54.833
We try to interpret his wishes
as best we can.

00:50:54.875 --> 00:50:56.934
I'm curious to know
how you've interpreted

00:50:56.977 --> 00:50:59.104
the Caretaker's reason
for sending us here.

00:50:59.146 --> 00:51:01.205
We believe he must
have separated you

00:51:01.248 --> 00:51:03.716
from your own species
for their protection.

00:51:03.751 --> 00:51:04.979
Their protection?

00:51:06.287 --> 00:51:07.481
From your illness.

00:51:08.789 --> 00:51:10.814
Perhaps he's trying
to prevent a plague.

00:51:10.858 --> 00:51:13.258
We weren't sick
until we met your Caretaker.

00:51:13.294 --> 00:51:16.354
From time to time,
he asks us to care for people

00:51:16.397 --> 00:51:17.523
with this disease.

00:51:17.565 --> 00:51:18.725
It's the least we can do.

00:51:18.766 --> 00:51:21.667
There have been others...
like us?

00:51:21.702 --> 00:51:23.670
Yes.

00:51:23.704 --> 00:51:25.569
Where are they?

00:51:27.875 --> 00:51:30.241
Your condition is serious.

00:51:30.277 --> 00:51:32.973
We don't know exactly
how to treat it.

00:51:33.047 --> 00:51:36.210
I'm afraid the others
did not recover.

00:52:29.737 --> 00:52:30.704
Sir...

00:52:30.738 --> 00:52:33.969
Ah, Mr. Vulcan.
Come in, come in.

00:52:34.008 --> 00:52:35.737
Please, I can hardly see you.

00:52:35.776 --> 00:52:39.473
I want to thank you
for your hospitality.

00:52:39.513 --> 00:52:42.539
I must admit,
I haven't had access

00:52:42.583 --> 00:52:45.074
to a food replor...
uh, replicator before.

00:52:46.220 --> 00:52:48.552
I'd never have guessed.

00:52:48.589 --> 00:52:50.147
And to immerse myself
in water...

00:52:50.190 --> 00:52:52.886
oh, do you know
what joy this is?

00:52:55.729 --> 00:52:58.425
No one around here
wastes water in this manner.

00:52:58.465 --> 00:52:59.989
A good sand scrub...

00:53:00.067 --> 00:53:01.659
that's the best
that we can hope for.

00:53:05.406 --> 00:53:07.636
I'm pleased
you're enjoying yourself,

00:53:07.675 --> 00:53:09.540
but we're in orbit
of the fifth planet.

00:53:09.576 --> 00:53:10.941
We need your assistance.

00:53:11.011 --> 00:53:14.037
Oh, uh, could you hand
me the, uh... towel?

00:53:20.120 --> 00:53:23.647
If you will scan
the large southern continent,

00:53:23.691 --> 00:53:25.716
you'll find a range
of extinct volcanoes.

00:53:25.759 --> 00:53:27.556
Follow the foothills north

00:53:27.594 --> 00:53:29.562
until you discover
a dry river bed.

00:53:29.596 --> 00:53:31.962
You'll find an encampment there.

00:53:31.999 --> 00:53:34.399
Do you believe our people
might be at this location?

00:53:34.435 --> 00:53:37.836
It's not impossible...
maybe...

00:53:39.206 --> 00:53:42.141
Perhaps not,
but we'll find them.

00:53:42.176 --> 00:53:45.703
We'll need several containers
of water to bring for barter.

00:53:45.746 --> 00:53:51.651
Do these, uh, replicators
make clothing, as well?

00:53:51.685 --> 00:53:53.152
Yes.

00:53:53.187 --> 00:53:55.917
Will it make me
a uniform like yours?

00:53:55.956 --> 00:53:57.287
No...

00:53:57.324 --> 00:53:59.155
it most certainly will not.

00:53:59.193 --> 00:54:00.387
Hmm.

00:54:27.654 --> 00:54:30.316
Why would anyone want
to live in a place like this?

00:54:30.357 --> 00:54:34.191
The rich cormaline deposits
are very much in demand.

00:54:34.228 --> 00:54:35.923
The Ocampa use it for barter?

00:54:35.963 --> 00:54:39.330
Not the Ocampa, the Kazon-Ogla.

00:54:39.366 --> 00:54:41.834
The Kazon-Ogla?
Who are the Kazon-Ogla?

00:54:41.869 --> 00:54:43.097
They are.

00:54:43.137 --> 00:54:45.697
Kazon sects control
this part of the Quadrant.

00:54:45.739 --> 00:54:48.333
Some have food, some have ore,
some have water.

00:54:48.375 --> 00:54:50.275
They all trade, and they all
kill each other for it.

00:54:50.310 --> 00:54:52.369
I thought you said the Ocampa
had our people.

00:54:52.413 --> 00:54:54.711
My friends!
It's good to see you again!

00:54:54.748 --> 00:54:56.045
Whoo!

00:54:59.420 --> 00:55:03.015
I must speak with your maje,
the ever-wise Jabin.

00:55:06.026 --> 00:55:08.256
Ah. Very amusing.

00:55:08.295 --> 00:55:09.853
Very amusing.

00:55:09.897 --> 00:55:11.728
I, uh...

00:55:11.765 --> 00:55:13.790
I enjoy a joke
as much as the next man.

00:55:15.469 --> 00:55:16.800
Jabin!

00:55:16.837 --> 00:55:17.769
My old friend!

00:55:21.074 --> 00:55:22.939
Water... water, Jabin.

00:55:22.976 --> 00:55:26.571
I have water... to replace
all that I borrowed.

00:55:26.613 --> 00:55:28.274
Show them, Mr. Paris.

00:55:28.315 --> 00:55:32.251
Their ship has technology that
makes water out of thin air!

00:55:41.395 --> 00:55:42.692
You have more?

00:55:42.729 --> 00:55:46.256
Janeway to Voyager.
Energize.

00:55:51.138 --> 00:55:52.298
Oh!

00:55:58.312 --> 00:56:01.372
There's more where that came
from if you can help us.

00:56:01.415 --> 00:56:03.542
How can we help someone
so powerful

00:56:03.584 --> 00:56:05.347
they can create water
out of thin air?

00:56:05.385 --> 00:56:07.546
This man led us here

00:56:07.588 --> 00:56:10.785
suggesting we might find
a people called the Ocampa.

00:56:10.824 --> 00:56:12.358
Do you know where they are?

00:56:12.491 --> 00:56:14.220
Ocampa?

00:56:15.828 --> 00:56:17.125
She is Ocampa.

00:56:17.162 --> 00:56:20.598
Why would you be interested
in such worthless creatures?

00:56:20.632 --> 00:56:22.099
They live only nine years.

00:56:22.134 --> 00:56:24.295
They make poor servants.

00:56:24.336 --> 00:56:26.236
We caught her when she wandered
to the surface.

00:56:26.271 --> 00:56:27.295
To the surface?

00:56:27.339 --> 00:56:29.330
You mean, they live underground?

00:56:29.375 --> 00:56:30.501
The entity in space

00:56:30.542 --> 00:56:32.772
that gives them food and power,
also gives them

00:56:32.811 --> 00:56:35.211
sole access to the only
water on this world...

00:56:35.247 --> 00:56:36.805
two miles below the surface.

00:56:36.849 --> 00:56:40.285
This same entity has abducted
two of our people.

00:56:40.319 --> 00:56:42.651
We believe they might be
with the Ocampa.

00:56:42.688 --> 00:56:46.249
There's no way to get to them.
We tried.

00:56:46.291 --> 00:56:47.724
The entity has established

00:56:47.760 --> 00:56:49.125
some kind
of subterranean barrier

00:56:49.161 --> 00:56:50.890
we cannot penetrate.

00:56:50.929 --> 00:56:52.328
But she got out.

00:56:52.364 --> 00:56:55.731
Occasionally, some of them do
find their way to the surface...

00:56:55.768 --> 00:56:57.395
we don't know how...

00:56:57.436 --> 00:56:59.666
but the Ocampa seal
the tunnels afterwards.

00:56:59.705 --> 00:57:03.038
Maybe she can help these
good people find a way down.

00:57:04.343 --> 00:57:07.141
You'd be wasting your time.

00:57:07.179 --> 00:57:08.271
I've used every method

00:57:08.313 --> 00:57:10.178
of persuasion I know
to get her to help us.

00:57:10.215 --> 00:57:12.012
She won't!

00:57:12.050 --> 00:57:13.608
Then she's worthless to you.

00:57:13.652 --> 00:57:18.055
Let us trade you water
for this scrawny little thing.

00:57:19.591 --> 00:57:23.322
I'd be more interested
in acquiring this technology

00:57:23.362 --> 00:57:26.126
that allows you to create water
from thin air.

00:57:26.165 --> 00:57:27.598
That would be difficult.

00:57:27.633 --> 00:57:30.534
It's integrated
into our ship's systems.

00:57:31.570 --> 00:57:32.696
Tell them to drop their weapons!

00:57:33.972 --> 00:57:36.440
Drop them, my friends,
or he dies in an instant.

00:57:36.475 --> 00:57:40.707
Do it!
Do it!

00:57:47.019 --> 00:57:48.179
Step aside.

00:57:54.660 --> 00:57:55.524
Come on!

00:57:57.663 --> 00:57:59.824
I strongly suggest
you get us out of here.

00:57:59.865 --> 00:58:01.162
Six to beam up.

00:58:12.344 --> 00:58:16.144
My dearest, didn't I promise
I'd save you?

00:58:31.730 --> 00:58:33.254
Look, I'm sure Captain Janeway

00:58:33.298 --> 00:58:35.493
is doing everything
she can to find us.

00:58:35.534 --> 00:58:38.128
What makes you think
any of them are still alive?

00:58:40.706 --> 00:58:42.674
Should I call for some help?

00:58:42.708 --> 00:58:44.107
No.

00:59:00.392 --> 00:59:02.019
Are you in pain?

00:59:02.060 --> 00:59:03.618
Are you watching us?

00:59:03.662 --> 00:59:05.391
I thought we weren't supposed
to be your prisoners.

00:59:05.430 --> 00:59:07.398
I wasn't watching you.

00:59:07.432 --> 00:59:08.865
I was coming
to give you something.

00:59:08.901 --> 00:59:10.129
I don't know if it will help.

00:59:10.168 --> 00:59:11.795
It's a medicine.

00:59:11.837 --> 00:59:13.236
There are people
who have broken

00:59:13.272 --> 00:59:14.899
from tradition
and left the city.

00:59:15.007 --> 00:59:17.305
Their colony
grows fruits and vegetables.

00:59:17.342 --> 00:59:19.867
They discovered quite by
accident that the moss

00:59:19.912 --> 00:59:21.470
that grows on
certain fruit trees

00:59:21.513 --> 00:59:22.639
has healing properties.

00:59:22.681 --> 00:59:25.582
I'm sorry for what
has happened to you.

00:59:25.617 --> 00:59:27.278
We appreciate this,

00:59:27.319 --> 00:59:28.616
but the only way
we're going to survive

00:59:28.654 --> 00:59:31.817
is if we can get to the surface
and find our own people.

00:59:31.857 --> 00:59:35.224
The elders would say that's
against the Caretaker's wishes.

00:59:35.260 --> 00:59:36.727
What do you say?

00:59:37.930 --> 00:59:39.898
The Caretaker's
been behaving strangely

00:59:39.932 --> 00:59:41.422
for the past several months...

00:59:41.466 --> 00:59:44.697
abducting people,
increasing the power supply.

00:59:44.736 --> 00:59:45.930
Power supply?

00:59:45.971 --> 00:59:48.098
He's tripled the energy
he sends us.

00:59:48.140 --> 00:59:49.937
They say we have
enough stored now

00:59:49.975 --> 00:59:51.636
to run the city for five years.

00:59:51.677 --> 00:59:53.508
And nobody knows why?

00:59:53.545 --> 00:59:58.608
When we ask, we're told to trust
the Caretaker's decisions.

00:59:58.650 --> 01:00:00.948
One person I knew
did get to the surface.

01:00:01.053 --> 01:00:02.953
We never saw her again.

01:00:02.988 --> 01:00:03.955
How?

01:00:03.989 --> 01:00:04.887
The ancient tunnels

01:00:04.923 --> 01:00:06.948
that brought us here
still exist.

01:00:07.025 --> 01:00:09.493
Over the years, small breaches
in security barriers

01:00:09.528 --> 01:00:10.825
have appeared,
just large enough

01:00:10.862 --> 01:00:13.296
for someone to get through,
but it still requires

01:00:13.332 --> 01:00:15.425
digging through meters
of rock to get out.

01:00:15.467 --> 01:00:17.958
Can you get us tools
to dig with?

01:00:18.003 --> 01:00:21.734
It would take days, maybe
even weeks to break through.

01:00:21.773 --> 01:00:23.968
You have to rest.

01:00:24.009 --> 01:00:25.306
Conserve your strength.

01:00:25.344 --> 01:00:27.972
Please... it's our only chance.

01:00:39.257 --> 01:00:41.418
If you had told us
what you had planned,

01:00:41.460 --> 01:00:43.985
we might have anticipated
your irrational behavior.

01:00:44.062 --> 01:00:46.326
Irrational?
We got out of there, didn't we?

01:00:46.365 --> 01:00:47.332
Excuse me.

01:00:47.366 --> 01:00:48.697
Don't blame Neelix...

01:00:48.734 --> 01:00:49.928
That's enough.

01:00:49.968 --> 01:00:52.334
This is a Sick Bay,
not a conference room.

01:00:52.371 --> 01:00:53.770
Visiting hours are over.

01:00:53.805 --> 01:00:57.366
Everyone, except my patient,
is to leave immediately.

01:00:57.409 --> 01:01:00.037
Computer, end medical
holographic program.

01:01:01.480 --> 01:01:03.880
I never should have
gone to the surface.

01:01:03.915 --> 01:01:05.940
I'm too curious.

01:01:05.984 --> 01:01:07.952
I'm told it's my worst failing.

01:01:07.986 --> 01:01:09.954
No, no.
It's a wonderful quality...

01:01:10.022 --> 01:01:11.512
your most endearing.

01:01:12.658 --> 01:01:14.387
Would you be willing
to take us underground

01:01:14.426 --> 01:01:15.620
to look for our missing crew?

01:01:15.661 --> 01:01:18.061
I'm afraid Jabin was right.

01:01:18.096 --> 01:01:19.529
There's no way to get down.

01:01:19.564 --> 01:01:21.361
The tunnel I came out
has been sealed.

01:01:21.400 --> 01:01:22.765
We don't need a tunnel.

01:01:22.801 --> 01:01:24.962
We have the ability
to transport there directly.

01:01:25.070 --> 01:01:28.972
Captain, our sensors did not
pick up any indication

01:01:29.007 --> 01:01:30.838
of an underground civilization.

01:01:30.876 --> 01:01:32.901
The subterranean barrier
Jabin described

01:01:32.944 --> 01:01:34.070
may be responsible.

01:01:34.112 --> 01:01:36.546
It might also block
our transporter.

01:01:36.581 --> 01:01:38.276
There are breaches

01:01:38.316 --> 01:01:41.513
in the security barrier
where it's begun to decay.

01:01:41.553 --> 01:01:42.952
That's how I got out.

01:01:44.389 --> 01:01:46.414
Have the transporter room
begin a sweep

01:01:46.458 --> 01:01:48.858
for any breaches we might
be able to beam through.

01:01:48.894 --> 01:01:51.328
Kes can tell you where to go,

01:01:51.363 --> 01:01:53.490
but, now that she's free,

01:01:53.532 --> 01:01:55.261
we're leaving
this system together.

01:01:55.300 --> 01:01:57.928
Neelix, these people rescued me.

01:01:57.969 --> 01:01:59.766
I rescued you.

01:01:59.805 --> 01:02:01.363
With their help.

01:02:01.406 --> 01:02:04.637
It would be wrong
not to help them now.

01:02:21.460 --> 01:02:22.893
Captain, the pulses
from the Array

01:02:22.928 --> 01:02:23.917
continue to accelerate.

01:02:23.962 --> 01:02:25.554
The intervals between them
have decreased

01:02:25.597 --> 01:02:27.121
another.8 seconds.

01:02:38.677 --> 01:02:40.076
Kes.

01:02:40.112 --> 01:02:41.079
Hello, Daggin.

01:02:41.113 --> 01:02:42.705
We thought we'd never
see you again.

01:02:42.748 --> 01:02:44.375
How did you get back?

01:02:44.416 --> 01:02:46.976
These people rescued me
from the Kazon.

01:02:47.018 --> 01:02:49.612
I'm trying to help them
find two of their crewmen.

01:02:49.654 --> 01:02:52.623
Does anyone know where
the aliens are kept... the ones

01:02:52.657 --> 01:02:54.249
the Caretaker sends here?

01:02:54.292 --> 01:02:55.589
I think they're
at the Central Clinic.

01:02:55.627 --> 01:02:57.185
Can you take us there?

01:02:57.229 --> 01:02:59.527
No, she cannot.

01:02:59.564 --> 01:03:01.395
They can't speak
telepathically, Toscat.

01:03:01.433 --> 01:03:04.129
Please talk aloud.

01:03:04.169 --> 01:03:06.603
I didn't mean to be rude,

01:03:06.638 --> 01:03:08.299
but you should not be here.

01:03:08.340 --> 01:03:11.173
We'll be glad to leave
once we find our crewmen.

01:03:11.209 --> 01:03:12.267
That won't be possible.

01:03:12.310 --> 01:03:14.437
We cannot interfere
with the Caretaker's wishes.

01:03:14.479 --> 01:03:16.709
Maybe you can't, but we can.

01:03:16.748 --> 01:03:18.045
You don't understand.

01:03:18.083 --> 01:03:19.175
That's right.

01:03:19.217 --> 01:03:20.684
They don't understand.

01:03:20.719 --> 01:03:21.947
They have no way of knowing

01:03:22.053 --> 01:03:23.714
that the Ocampa
have been dependent

01:03:23.755 --> 01:03:25.120
on the Caretaker for so long

01:03:25.157 --> 01:03:27.751
that we can't even think
for ourselves anymore.

01:03:27.793 --> 01:03:30.193
They don't understand
we were once a people

01:03:30.228 --> 01:03:33.163
who had full command
of our minds' abilities.

01:03:33.198 --> 01:03:36.133
The stories of our ancestors'
cognitive abilities

01:03:36.168 --> 01:03:37.226
are apocryphal...

01:03:37.269 --> 01:03:39.635
at the very least exaggerated.

01:03:39.671 --> 01:03:42.663
We lost those abilities
because we stopped using them.

01:03:42.707 --> 01:03:45.198
We should not dwell
on what's been lost,

01:03:45.243 --> 01:03:46.835
but on all that's been gained.

01:03:46.878 --> 01:03:48.971
We've gained a talent
for dependence,

01:03:49.080 --> 01:03:51.173
for simply taking
what we're given.

01:03:51.216 --> 01:03:53.514
I'm going to help them, Toscat,
whether you like it or not,

01:03:53.552 --> 01:03:56.248
and I think my friends
will join me.

01:04:00.992 --> 01:04:03.552
You defied the Caretaker
by going to the surface, Kes.

01:04:03.595 --> 01:04:06.655
Learn from the experience.

01:04:06.698 --> 01:04:08.666
Follow the path
he has set for us.

01:04:08.700 --> 01:04:10.895
I've learned very well, Toscat.

01:04:10.936 --> 01:04:13.131
I saw the sunlight.

01:04:13.171 --> 01:04:14.934
I can't believe
that our Caretaker

01:04:14.973 --> 01:04:17.066
would forbid us
to open our eyes

01:04:17.108 --> 01:04:18.905
and see the sky.

01:04:18.944 --> 01:04:21.378
Come with me...
we'll find your people.

01:04:42.834 --> 01:04:43.926
Come on.

01:04:59.217 --> 01:05:01.913
Don't let it beat you,
Starfleet. Come on.

01:05:01.953 --> 01:05:02.942
I'm sorry.

01:05:08.426 --> 01:05:10.087
All right.

01:05:12.097 --> 01:05:14.895
It's all right.
We'll rest a minute.

01:05:14.933 --> 01:05:17.868
Maybe I'd do better if I had
a little Klingon blood in me.

01:05:17.903 --> 01:05:22.135
Trust me... it's more trouble
than it's worth.

01:05:22.173 --> 01:05:25.074
You know, I spent my whole life
getting ready for Starfleet,

01:05:25.110 --> 01:05:28.944
and on my very first mission,

01:05:29.014 --> 01:05:31.812
I'm going to die.

01:05:31.850 --> 01:05:34.444
We're not finished yet.

01:05:36.121 --> 01:05:39.147
I know a few things
that old Sneezy didn't teach

01:05:39.190 --> 01:05:40.214
in his survival course.

01:05:40.258 --> 01:05:41.225
Sneezy?

01:05:41.259 --> 01:05:43.386
Commander Zakarian.

01:05:43.428 --> 01:05:44.395
Remember?

01:05:44.429 --> 01:05:47.694
He must have been
allergic to everything.

01:05:47.732 --> 01:05:49.131
You went to the Academy.

01:05:49.167 --> 01:05:52.659
I actually made it into the
second year before we, uh...

01:05:52.704 --> 01:05:55.764
we mutually agreed
that it wasn't the place for me.

01:05:55.807 --> 01:05:56.774
You know

01:05:56.808 --> 01:05:59.242
I never really liked Zakarian.

01:06:00.979 --> 01:06:02.946
Shh. Listen.

01:06:03.079 --> 01:06:05.343
They're getting faster.

01:06:19.963 --> 01:06:21.225
Away team to Voyager.

01:06:21.264 --> 01:06:22.231
Voyager here.

01:06:22.265 --> 01:06:23.892
What's going on with the Array?

01:06:23.933 --> 01:06:26.424
It's no longer
sending out pulses, Captain,

01:06:26.469 --> 01:06:29.029
and it appears to be
realigning its position.

01:06:29.072 --> 01:06:31.097
Keep me informed.
Janeway out.

01:06:35.511 --> 01:06:37.741
They haven't been
at the clinic for hours.

01:06:37.780 --> 01:06:39.577
We can search the city.
Ask if anyone's seen them.

01:06:39.615 --> 01:06:42.140
If they were trying to get to
the surface, how would they go?

01:06:42.185 --> 01:06:45.086
Probably the same way I did...
up one of the ancient tunnels.

01:06:46.222 --> 01:06:47.883
Mr. Paris,
you and Neelix go with her

01:06:47.924 --> 01:06:49.255
and start checking them out.

01:06:50.593 --> 01:06:53.061
We need to talk to every doctor
and nurse at this hospital

01:06:53.096 --> 01:06:54.996
see what they can tell us
about Torres and Kim.

01:06:56.032 --> 01:06:57.158
Voyager to Janeway.

01:06:57.200 --> 01:06:58.167
Go ahead.

01:06:58.201 --> 01:06:59.293
Captain, the Array

01:06:59.335 --> 01:07:01.633
is firing some kind of weapon
at the surface.

01:07:01.671 --> 01:07:04.902
It seems to be trying to seal
the energy conduits.

01:07:05.008 --> 01:07:07.203
Understood.
Keep a channel open.

01:07:08.378 --> 01:07:10.539
If the Array is the Ocampa's
sole source of energy,

01:07:10.580 --> 01:07:12.480
why would the Caretaker
seal the conduits?

01:07:12.515 --> 01:07:13.482
He would seal them

01:07:13.516 --> 01:07:14.744
if he no longer
intended to use them

01:07:14.784 --> 01:07:16.843
to protect the Ocampa
from their enemies.

01:07:16.886 --> 01:07:18.285
Captain, there is
now enough evidence

01:07:18.321 --> 01:07:20.084
to form a reasonable
hypothesis.

01:07:20.123 --> 01:07:22.023
I believe that
the Caretaker is dying.

01:07:22.058 --> 01:07:23.150
Explain.

01:07:23.192 --> 01:07:25.422
First, he increases
the energy supply

01:07:25.461 --> 01:07:27.122
to provide the city
with a surplus

01:07:27.163 --> 01:07:30.030
to last at least five years,
then he seals the conduits.

01:07:30.066 --> 01:07:32.091
The logical conclusion is
that he does not intend

01:07:32.135 --> 01:07:34.035
to continue his role
as Caretaker.

01:07:34.070 --> 01:07:35.628
That doesn't necessarily
mean he's dying.

01:07:35.671 --> 01:07:36.729
He could be leaving.

01:07:36.773 --> 01:07:38.570
Doubtful.

01:07:38.608 --> 01:07:41.042
Not after a millennium
of providing for these people.

01:07:41.077 --> 01:07:44.274
I believe that the Caretaker
owes something to the Ocampa.

01:07:44.313 --> 01:07:45.940
I believe the "debt
that can never be repaid"

01:07:45.982 --> 01:07:48.314
is very likely a debt to them.

01:07:48.351 --> 01:07:50.581
In addition, there were
his frequent references

01:07:50.620 --> 01:07:52.212
to "running out of time."

01:07:52.255 --> 01:07:54.746
I think he knew
his death was imminent.

01:07:54.791 --> 01:07:58.955
If he dies, how the hell
are we supposed to get home?

01:08:06.803 --> 01:08:08.430
They're in this one.

01:08:08.471 --> 01:08:10.336
Harry?!

01:08:12.341 --> 01:08:13.467
Paris to Janeway.

01:08:13.509 --> 01:08:14.533
Go ahead.

01:08:14.577 --> 01:08:16.568
They're in one
of the tunnels, Captain.

01:08:16.612 --> 01:08:19.103
I can't see them,
but they're up there.

01:08:19.148 --> 01:08:20.638
We're going after them.

01:08:20.683 --> 01:08:22.913
Call for transport
when you have them, Paris.

01:08:22.952 --> 01:08:24.351
We'll meet you on the ship.

01:08:24.387 --> 01:08:26.321
Janeway to Voyager.

01:08:26.355 --> 01:08:27.322
Voyager here.

01:08:27.356 --> 01:08:28.345
Three to beam up.

01:08:28.391 --> 01:08:29.619
Stand by.

01:08:31.394 --> 01:08:33.385
Captain,
I can't get a lock on you.

01:08:33.429 --> 01:08:35.158
The weapons fire from the Array

01:08:35.198 --> 01:08:36.927
has irradiated
the planet's crust.

01:08:36.966 --> 01:08:39.127
The transport sensors
can't find the breaches

01:08:39.168 --> 01:08:40.396
in the security barrier.

01:08:41.504 --> 01:08:43.836
Come on, there's only one
other way out of here.

01:08:45.875 --> 01:08:47.069
Janeway to Paris.

01:08:47.110 --> 01:08:48.304
Go ahead.

01:08:48.344 --> 01:08:50.369
The transporters aren't working.

01:08:50.413 --> 01:08:52.677
You're going to have to find
a breach in the security barrier

01:08:52.715 --> 01:08:54.046
when you get to the top.

01:08:55.184 --> 01:08:56.651
Understood.

01:08:56.686 --> 01:08:58.210
We're a few minutes behind you.

01:08:58.254 --> 01:08:59.243
Janeway out.

01:09:02.058 --> 01:09:03.719
I see them.

01:09:15.938 --> 01:09:17.701
Took you long enough.

01:09:17.740 --> 01:09:20.573
How could I let down
the only friend I got?

01:09:20.610 --> 01:09:23.078
Friend? What makes
you think I'm your friend?

01:09:25.648 --> 01:09:27.172
Paris to Janeway.

01:09:27.216 --> 01:09:28.183
Go ahead.

01:09:28.217 --> 01:09:29.184
We found them, Captain.

01:09:29.218 --> 01:09:30.310
Don't wait for us.

01:09:30.353 --> 01:09:31.342
Get them to safety.

01:09:36.492 --> 01:09:37.459
Don't worry.

01:09:37.493 --> 01:09:39.620
I know where we can
get through the barrier.

01:09:47.036 --> 01:09:49.334
Whatever you do, don't touch it.

01:09:49.372 --> 01:09:52.398
We've been told
it'll burn your skin off.

01:10:07.156 --> 01:10:08.555
They're not far ahead of us.

01:10:08.591 --> 01:10:09.649
Keep going.

01:10:27.109 --> 01:10:29.304
I think we've reached the top.

01:10:29.345 --> 01:10:32.576
Neelix, get out your phaser.

01:11:39.282 --> 01:11:42.217
Voyager, can you get
a lock on us now?

01:11:42.251 --> 01:11:44.811
Affirmative, but I'm reading
only five signals.

01:11:44.854 --> 01:11:46.378
The others are...

01:11:46.422 --> 01:11:47.855
Get down!

01:11:59.302 --> 01:12:01.429
Paris to Janeway.

01:12:01.470 --> 01:12:04.871
Chakotay, Tuvok, do you read?

01:12:06.275 --> 01:12:07.674
Voyager, prepare to transport

01:12:07.710 --> 01:12:09.041
everyone in this group
except me.

01:12:09.078 --> 01:12:10.170
Aye, sir.

01:12:10.212 --> 01:12:11.679
You're not thinking
of going back there.

01:12:17.486 --> 01:12:18.475
Well...

01:12:18.521 --> 01:12:20.284
the fool needs company.

01:12:20.323 --> 01:12:21.722
Take care of them, dearest.

01:12:21.757 --> 01:12:23.122
I'll see you later.

01:12:23.159 --> 01:12:25.753
Voyager, make that
three to beam up.

01:12:25.795 --> 01:12:29.253
Lock in on the other combadge
and energize.

01:12:38.808 --> 01:12:40.332
My leg is broken.

01:12:40.376 --> 01:12:42.276
I can't move.

01:12:42.311 --> 01:12:43.744
- Hold on.
- Here they are!

01:12:43.779 --> 01:12:45.576
Neelix, help me with Tuvok.

01:12:48.551 --> 01:12:49.984
I'll get Chakotay.

01:13:06.102 --> 01:13:07.069
Get out of here, Paris,

01:13:07.103 --> 01:13:08.934
before the whole thing
comes down!

01:13:09.038 --> 01:13:10.767
I intend to...

01:13:10.806 --> 01:13:12.068
as soon as I get you up.

01:13:12.108 --> 01:13:14.542
You get on those stairs,
they'll collapse.

01:13:14.577 --> 01:13:16.408
We'll both die.

01:13:16.445 --> 01:13:18.037
Yeah...

01:13:18.080 --> 01:13:19.513
but on the other hand,

01:13:19.548 --> 01:13:22.142
if I save your butt,
your life belongs to me.

01:13:32.128 --> 01:13:34.323
Isn't that some kind
of Indian custom?

01:13:35.965 --> 01:13:37.364
Wrong tribe.

01:13:39.535 --> 01:13:41.503
I don't believe you.

01:13:46.542 --> 01:13:49.477
You'd rather die than let me
be the one to rescue you.

01:13:51.447 --> 01:13:53.745
Fine. Be a fool.

01:13:53.783 --> 01:13:55.580
If I have to die,

01:13:55.618 --> 01:13:58.052
at least I'll have the pleasure
of watching you go with me.

01:14:03.159 --> 01:14:05.024
Isn't there some Indian trick

01:14:05.060 --> 01:14:07.290
where you can turn
yourself into a bird

01:14:07.329 --> 01:14:09.422
and fly us out of here?

01:14:09.465 --> 01:14:11.296
You're too heavy.

01:14:33.522 --> 01:14:35.285
Bridge to Janeway.

01:14:35.324 --> 01:14:36.416
Go ahead.

01:14:36.459 --> 01:14:38.757
Captain, two Kazon ships
are approaching the Array.

01:14:38.794 --> 01:14:40.591
Set a course.
I'm on my way.

01:14:40.629 --> 01:14:42.062
We've got to get back
to our ship.

01:14:42.097 --> 01:14:45.396
I strongly advise you to rest.

01:14:45.434 --> 01:14:47.595
I will not be held responsible
for the consequences.

01:14:47.636 --> 01:14:49.968
Is the crew always
this difficult?

01:14:50.005 --> 01:14:50.972
I don't know, Doc.

01:14:51.006 --> 01:14:52.166
It's my first mission.

01:14:57.346 --> 01:14:59.177
Doesn't anyone know how
to turn off the program

01:14:59.215 --> 01:15:00.204
when they leave?

01:15:02.051 --> 01:15:03.916
Bring the weapons systems
on line.

01:15:03.953 --> 01:15:07.013
Powering up phaser banks
and photon systems.

01:15:08.224 --> 01:15:09.350
Red Alert.

01:15:27.443 --> 01:15:29.104
The lead Kazon ship
is hailing us, Captain.

01:15:29.144 --> 01:15:30.475
On screen.

01:15:30.513 --> 01:15:32.242
Have you come to investigate

01:15:32.281 --> 01:15:34.545
the Entity's strange behavior
too, Captain?

01:15:34.583 --> 01:15:36.949
All we care about
is getting home, Jabin.

01:15:36.986 --> 01:15:38.851
We're about to transport
over to the Array

01:15:38.888 --> 01:15:40.150
to see if we can arrange it.

01:15:40.189 --> 01:15:41.952
I'm afraid I cannot permit that.

01:15:42.057 --> 01:15:44.321
We have no dispute with you.

01:15:44.360 --> 01:15:46.157
I have a dispute with anyone
who would challenge us.

01:15:46.195 --> 01:15:47.958
This is ridiculous.

01:15:48.063 --> 01:15:49.894
We have no intention
of challenging you.

01:15:49.932 --> 01:15:51.923
And I have no intention
of letting anyone

01:15:51.967 --> 01:15:54.197
with your technological
knowledge board the Array.

01:15:54.236 --> 01:15:57.763
Jabin, can we discuss this
like two civilized?

01:15:57.806 --> 01:15:59.831
They're powering up
their weapons.

01:15:59.875 --> 01:16:01.240
I guess we can't.

01:16:03.145 --> 01:16:05.409
Shields are holding.

01:16:06.782 --> 01:16:10.051
Fire phasers.
Evasive pattern delta four.

01:16:24.899 --> 01:16:26.491
Janeway to Chakotay.

01:16:26.534 --> 01:16:28.297
Tuvok and I
are beaming to the Array.

01:16:28.335 --> 01:16:30.098
Can you hold off the Kazon?

01:16:30.137 --> 01:16:31.570
I think so, Captain.

01:16:31.605 --> 01:16:32.902
Good.

01:16:32.940 --> 01:16:36.171
Mr. Paris, take the conn.

01:16:37.378 --> 01:16:39.039
Yes, ma'am.

01:16:39.080 --> 01:16:40.513
Maintain transporter locks,
Ensign.

01:16:40.548 --> 01:16:41.515
Emergency beam out status.

01:16:41.549 --> 01:16:42.538
Aye, Captain.

01:16:56.130 --> 01:16:59.031
The data processing system
is behind this wall, Captain.

01:17:04.939 --> 01:17:06.270
You know what to do.

01:17:26.227 --> 01:17:31.221
Well... you're, you're nothing
if not persistent.

01:17:31.265 --> 01:17:34.257
We need you to send us back
where we came from.

01:17:34.301 --> 01:17:37.429
Oh... that isn't possible.

01:17:37.471 --> 01:17:41.965
I have... barely enough strength
to complete my work.

01:17:44.345 --> 01:17:47.473
You're sealing the conduits
before you die.

01:17:47.515 --> 01:17:52.145
If I don't, the Kazon
will steal the water.

01:17:52.186 --> 01:17:55.155
But, in a few years,

01:17:55.189 --> 01:17:58.818
when the Ocampa's energy
runs out, it won't matter.

01:17:58.859 --> 01:18:01.384
They'll be forced
to come to the surface

01:18:01.428 --> 01:18:03.896
and they won't be able
to survive.

01:18:03.964 --> 01:18:07.263
Something you did turned
their planet into a desert,

01:18:07.301 --> 01:18:08.359
didn't it?

01:18:08.402 --> 01:18:11.132
That was the debt
that could never be repaid.

01:18:11.172 --> 01:18:16.735
Well, we're explorers
from another galaxy,

01:18:16.777 --> 01:18:20.076
but we had no idea
that our technology

01:18:20.114 --> 01:18:23.845
would be so destructive
to their atmosphere.

01:18:23.884 --> 01:18:25.511
Two, two of us

01:18:25.553 --> 01:18:29.216
were chosen to stay
behind and care for them.

01:18:29.256 --> 01:18:30.951
There's another like you here?

01:18:32.526 --> 01:18:34.585
Not anymore.

01:18:34.628 --> 01:18:36.425
No, no. She...

01:18:36.463 --> 01:18:39.523
she went off to look
for more interesting places.

01:18:39.567 --> 01:18:41.398
Why were you bringing
ships here...

01:18:41.435 --> 01:18:43.767
infecting people
with a fatal illness?

01:18:43.804 --> 01:18:44.793
Oh, they...

01:18:44.838 --> 01:18:47.932
they didn't die of an illness.

01:18:48.042 --> 01:18:54.140
They died
because they were incompatible.

01:18:55.282 --> 01:18:57.045
"Incompatible"?

01:18:57.084 --> 01:18:59.746
I've been searching the galaxy

01:18:59.787 --> 01:19:04.281
for a compatible
biomolecular pattern.

01:19:04.325 --> 01:19:06.156
Now, in some individuals,

01:19:06.193 --> 01:19:09.890
I found cellular structures
that were similar, but I...

01:19:09.964 --> 01:19:11.864
You've been trying to procreate?

01:19:11.899 --> 01:19:15.062
I needed someone to replace me...

01:19:15.102 --> 01:19:16.763
someone who'd understand

01:19:16.804 --> 01:19:22.436
the enormous responsibility
of... caring for the Ocampa.

01:19:22.476 --> 01:19:25.775
Only my offspring could do that.

01:19:32.686 --> 01:19:35.416
Did you ever consider
allowing the Ocampa

01:19:35.456 --> 01:19:37.253
to care for themselves?

01:19:39.059 --> 01:19:40.754
They're children.

01:19:40.794 --> 01:19:42.728
Children have to grow up.

01:19:42.763 --> 01:19:45.459
We're explorers, too.

01:19:45.499 --> 01:19:46.932
Most of the species
we've encountered

01:19:46.967 --> 01:19:48.764
have overcome all kinds
of adversity

01:19:48.802 --> 01:19:50.326
without a Caretaker.

01:19:50.371 --> 01:19:52.737
It's the challenge
of surviving on their own

01:19:52.773 --> 01:19:54.673
that helps them to evolve.

01:19:54.708 --> 01:20:00.578
Maybe your... children
will do better than you think.

01:20:01.749 --> 01:20:03.546
Voyager to Janeway.

01:20:03.584 --> 01:20:04.573
Go ahead.

01:20:04.618 --> 01:20:05.880
We've got problems here.

01:20:16.263 --> 01:20:17.628
Kazon just got some backup.

01:20:17.665 --> 01:20:19.292
We need more time.

01:20:19.333 --> 01:20:21.563
Can you hold them off
for another few minutes?

01:20:21.602 --> 01:20:23.433
We'll do our best.
Kim out.

01:20:24.638 --> 01:20:26.765
Their weapons array
has been hit.

01:20:27.775 --> 01:20:28.901
They're in trouble.

01:20:28.942 --> 01:20:32.810
Neither of us has enough
firepower to stop that ship.

01:20:32.846 --> 01:20:34.245
I'm setting a collision course,

01:20:34.281 --> 01:20:36.511
but the guidance
system is disabled.

01:20:36.550 --> 01:20:38.745
I'll have to pilot
the ship manually.

01:20:38.786 --> 01:20:40.777
Get the crew ready
to beam to Voyager

01:20:40.821 --> 01:20:42.550
and drop shields for transport.

01:20:44.458 --> 01:20:46.358
Paris, my crew is coming over.

01:20:46.393 --> 01:20:49.487
Tell one of your crackerjack
Starfleet transporter chiefs

01:20:49.530 --> 01:20:50.861
to keep a lock on me.

01:20:50.898 --> 01:20:53.162
I'm going to try and take
some heat off your tail.

01:20:53.200 --> 01:20:54.690
Acknowledged.

01:20:54.735 --> 01:20:57.533
But don't think for a second
this makes us even, Chakotay.

01:20:57.571 --> 01:20:59.471
Your life is still mine.

01:20:59.506 --> 01:21:01.337
Paris out.

01:21:07.614 --> 01:21:09.206
I'm holding a lock on him, sir,

01:21:09.249 --> 01:21:10.944
but he's getting too close.

01:21:12.019 --> 01:21:13.646
I'm getting you out
of there, Chakotay.

01:21:13.687 --> 01:21:14.711
Not yet!

01:21:19.093 --> 01:21:20.355
You're breaking up!

01:21:20.394 --> 01:21:21.588
Stand by to transport.

01:21:21.628 --> 01:21:23.220
Wait!

01:21:30.871 --> 01:21:32.031
Now!

01:21:40.280 --> 01:21:42.441
Transporter Room 2,
do you have him?

01:21:42.483 --> 01:21:43.882
They've got me.

01:21:53.494 --> 01:21:56.088
Captain, I can access the system

01:21:56.130 --> 01:21:57.791
to send us back
to Federation space,

01:21:57.831 --> 01:22:00.129
but it will take
several hours to activate.

01:22:01.368 --> 01:22:03.097
Unless you help us.

01:22:03.137 --> 01:22:05.230
Oh, I wish I could,

01:22:05.272 --> 01:22:08.036
but I have
very little time left.

01:22:08.075 --> 01:22:11.943
So I have initiated
a self-destruct program.

01:22:12.012 --> 01:22:15.072
If you destroy the Array,
we'll have no way to get home.

01:22:15.115 --> 01:22:17.083
The Ocampa's enemies
cannot be allowed

01:22:17.117 --> 01:22:20.052
to, to control
this installation.

01:22:20.087 --> 01:22:23.614
In minutes,
it will be destroyed.

01:22:23.657 --> 01:22:25.522
You have to go.

01:22:25.559 --> 01:22:27.424
Go now!

01:22:51.752 --> 01:22:54.243
The Caretaker.

01:22:57.758 --> 01:22:59.487
Voyager, report.

01:22:59.526 --> 01:23:00.493
A Kazon vessel

01:23:00.527 --> 01:23:02.893
just collided
with the Array, Captain.

01:23:02.930 --> 01:23:04.761
Are you all right?

01:23:04.798 --> 01:23:05.924
Affirmative.

01:23:05.966 --> 01:23:07.593
Stand by.

01:23:07.634 --> 01:23:10.728
The self-destruct program
has been damaged.

01:23:10.771 --> 01:23:14.263
Now, this installation
will not be destroyed.

01:23:14.308 --> 01:23:15.536
But it must be.

01:23:15.576 --> 01:23:20.377
The Kazon must not be allowed
to gain control of it.

01:23:20.414 --> 01:23:23.577
They will annihilate the Ocampa.

01:23:47.140 --> 01:23:49.540
Shall I activate
the program to get us back?

01:23:49.576 --> 01:23:53.171
And what happens to the Ocampa
after we're gone?

01:23:56.850 --> 01:24:01.913
Captain, any action we take
to protect the Ocampa

01:24:01.989 --> 01:24:05.015
would affect the balance
of power in this system.

01:24:05.058 --> 01:24:08.926
The Prime Directive
would seem to apply.

01:24:09.029 --> 01:24:10.519
Would it?

01:24:13.467 --> 01:24:16.027
We never asked to be involved,
Tuvok...

01:24:18.539 --> 01:24:20.632
but we are.

01:24:22.342 --> 01:24:24.139
We are.

01:24:30.751 --> 01:24:33.584
Mr. Tuvok, ready
the tricobalt devices.

01:24:33.620 --> 01:24:34.279
Aye, Captain.

01:24:34.321 --> 01:24:35.754
Open a channel to the Kazon.

01:24:35.789 --> 01:24:36.949
Channel open.

01:24:36.990 --> 01:24:38.480
Be advised, Captain.

01:24:38.525 --> 01:24:40.459
I have called
for additional ships.

01:24:40.494 --> 01:24:43.952
I'm calling to warn you to move
your vessels to a safe distance.

01:24:43.997 --> 01:24:46.329
I intend to destroy the Array.

01:24:46.366 --> 01:24:47.833
You can't do that.

01:24:47.868 --> 01:24:49.859
I can and I will.

01:24:49.903 --> 01:24:51.598
End transmission.

01:24:52.439 --> 01:24:54.737
They're increasing fire,
Captain.

01:24:54.775 --> 01:24:55.935
Shields are holding.

01:24:55.976 --> 01:24:58.308
Move us 400 kilometers
from the Array, Mr. Paris.

01:24:58.345 --> 01:24:59.972
Yes, ma'am.

01:25:00.047 --> 01:25:01.207
What do you think you're doing?

01:25:01.248 --> 01:25:03.614
That Array is the only way
we have to get back home.

01:25:03.650 --> 01:25:05.618
I'm aware everyone has
families and loved ones

01:25:05.652 --> 01:25:07.176
at homes they want
to get back to...

01:25:07.220 --> 01:25:10.212
so do l... but I'm not
willing to trade the lives

01:25:10.257 --> 01:25:12.350
of the Ocampa
for our convenience.

01:25:12.392 --> 01:25:13.916
We'll have to find
another way home.

01:25:14.027 --> 01:25:15.688
What other way home is there?

01:25:15.729 --> 01:25:18.857
Who is she to be making
these decisions for all of us?

01:25:18.899 --> 01:25:20.628
She's the Captain.

01:25:22.069 --> 01:25:24.503
The tricobalt devices are ready.

01:25:24.538 --> 01:25:26.665
We're in position.

01:25:32.079 --> 01:25:33.774
Fire.

01:25:57.904 --> 01:26:00.839
The lead Kazon ship
is hailing us.

01:26:00.874 --> 01:26:02.808
On screen.

01:26:04.511 --> 01:26:06.741
You have made an enemy today.

01:26:09.383 --> 01:26:11.578
They are withdrawing, Captain.

01:26:21.595 --> 01:26:22.926
Come in.

01:26:25.732 --> 01:26:27.563
You asked to see me, Captain?

01:26:27.601 --> 01:26:29.728
Mr. Paris...

01:26:29.770 --> 01:26:31.738
you have a problem.

01:26:31.772 --> 01:26:34.070
I've invited Chakotay

01:26:34.107 --> 01:26:36.675
and the other Maquis
to become part of this crew.

01:26:36.808 --> 01:26:38.400
It seemed the only
reasonable thing to do

01:26:38.443 --> 01:26:39.933
under the circumstances.

01:26:40.045 --> 01:26:42.536
Will you provide
a bodyguard for me, Captain?

01:26:42.580 --> 01:26:44.343
It seems you already have one.

01:26:44.382 --> 01:26:46.213
I do?

01:26:46.251 --> 01:26:49.914
Mr. Chakotay said something
about his life belonging to you.

01:26:49.954 --> 01:26:52.946
He'll be taking responsibility
for your safety.

01:26:52.991 --> 01:26:56.392
I think I'm going to enjoy this.

01:26:56.428 --> 01:26:58.419
Don't be so sure.

01:26:58.463 --> 01:27:00.556
He'll also be my First Officer.

01:27:00.598 --> 01:27:03.362
Everyone aboard this ship
will report to him...

01:27:03.401 --> 01:27:07.269
including the Lieutenant
assigned to conn.

01:27:08.907 --> 01:27:10.204
Me?

01:27:10.241 --> 01:27:13.540
I've entered into the Ship's Log
on this date

01:27:13.578 --> 01:27:16.638
that I'm granting
a field commission of Lieutenant

01:27:16.681 --> 01:27:18.672
to Thomas Eugene Paris.

01:27:23.788 --> 01:27:24.880
Congratulations.

01:27:27.992 --> 01:27:30.290
Um, for the first time
in my life,

01:27:30.328 --> 01:27:32.159
I don't know what to say.

01:27:32.197 --> 01:27:34.597
You've earned this, Tom.

01:27:34.632 --> 01:27:37.192
I'm only sorry
your father won't know.

01:27:37.235 --> 01:27:38.725
Oh, he'll know...

01:27:41.072 --> 01:27:42.664
when we get back.

01:27:42.707 --> 01:27:46.234
Ah, Captain, we were
just coming to see you.

01:27:46.277 --> 01:27:48.268
We've supplied your ship
with water, Neelix.

01:27:48.313 --> 01:27:49.575
It's ready to go.

01:27:49.614 --> 01:27:52.947
Well, you see that's what
we wanted to discuss.

01:27:53.051 --> 01:27:55.212
We'd like to go with you.

01:27:56.287 --> 01:27:58.687
I'm sorry.
This isn't a passenger ship.

01:27:58.723 --> 01:27:59.712
Of course not.

01:27:59.758 --> 01:28:00.782
We won't be passengers.

01:28:00.825 --> 01:28:03.055
We'd be valuable colleagues.

01:28:03.094 --> 01:28:04.288
"Colleagues"?

01:28:04.329 --> 01:28:07.594
Whatever you need is
what I have to offer.

01:28:07.632 --> 01:28:10.157
You need a guide,
I'm your guide.

01:28:10.201 --> 01:28:13.102
You need supplies, I know
where to procure them.

01:28:13.138 --> 01:28:16.801
I have friends among races
you don't even know exist.

01:28:16.841 --> 01:28:17.808
You need a cook?

01:28:17.842 --> 01:28:19.070
Oh, you haven't lived

01:28:19.110 --> 01:28:21.271
until you've tasted
my angla'bosque.

01:28:21.312 --> 01:28:24.475
It will be my job
to anticipate your needs

01:28:24.516 --> 01:28:26.006
before you know you have them.

01:28:26.050 --> 01:28:28.382
And I anticipate your first need

01:28:28.419 --> 01:28:30.114
will be me.

01:28:30.155 --> 01:28:32.282
Captain, we both want

01:28:32.323 --> 01:28:34.518
very much to be a part
of your journey.

01:28:49.974 --> 01:28:55.276
We're alone in
an uncharted part of the galaxy.

01:28:55.313 --> 01:28:58.908
We've already made
some friends here

01:28:58.950 --> 01:29:01.009
and some enemies.

01:29:01.052 --> 01:29:05.455
We have no idea of the dangers
we're going to face,

01:29:05.490 --> 01:29:08.084
but one thing is clear:

01:29:08.126 --> 01:29:11.095
Both crews are going
to have to work together

01:29:11.129 --> 01:29:13.654
if we're to survive.

01:29:13.698 --> 01:29:16.758
That's why Commander Chakotay
and I have agreed

01:29:16.801 --> 01:29:18.428
that this should be one crew...

01:29:20.104 --> 01:29:21.731
a Starfleet crew.

01:29:21.773 --> 01:29:25.903
And as the only Starfleet vessel
assigned to the Delta Quadrant

01:29:26.010 --> 01:29:28.274
we'll continue
to follow our directive

01:29:28.313 --> 01:29:31.578
to seek out new worlds
and explore space.

01:29:34.485 --> 01:29:37.454
But our primary goal is clear.

01:29:37.488 --> 01:29:39.388
Even at maximum speeds

01:29:39.424 --> 01:29:43.019
it would take 75 years
to reach the Federation,

01:29:43.061 --> 01:29:46.497
but I'm not willing
to settle for that.

01:29:46.531 --> 01:29:49.591
There's another entity
like the Caretaker

01:29:49.634 --> 01:29:50.862
out there somewhere

01:29:50.902 --> 01:29:53.700
who has the ability
to get us there a lot faster.

01:29:53.738 --> 01:29:55.569
We'll be looking for her

01:29:55.607 --> 01:29:59.043
and we'll be looking
for wormholes, spatial rifts

01:29:59.077 --> 01:30:01.511
or new technologies to help us.

01:30:03.514 --> 01:30:07.917
Somewhere, along this journey,

01:30:07.952 --> 01:30:10.887
we'll find a way back.

01:30:11.956 --> 01:30:15.619
Mr. Paris, set a course...

01:30:15.660 --> 01:30:18.060
for home.

01:30:18.096 --> 01:30:19.120
Aye, Captain.
